WEBVTT


00:00:42.994 --> 00:00:45.034
<i>Report
to your stations immediately.</i>


00:00:45.154 --> 00:00:46.758
<i>This is not a drill.</i>


00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:47.915
<i>We are under attack!</i>


00:00:49.314 --> 00:00:51.282
<i>We are under attack!</i>


00:01:52.394 --> 00:01:54.681
- Shit!
- Language!


00:01:54.794 --> 00:01:56.398
Jarvis, what's the view from upstairs?


00:01:56.794 --> 00:01:57.841
<i>The central building is</i>


00:01:57.954 --> 00:02:00.480
<i>protected by some kind
of energy shield.</i>


00:02:00.994 --> 00:02:02.439
<i>Strucker's technology is well beyond</i>


00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:04.716
<i>any other Hydra base we've taken.</i>


00:02:07.554 --> 00:02:09.124
Loki's sceptre must be here.


00:02:09.754 --> 00:02:11.634
Strucker couldn't
mount this defence without it.


00:02:12.354 --> 00:02:13.924
At long last.


00:02:25.394 --> 00:02:27.601
"At long last" is lasting
a little long, boys.


00:02:32.514 --> 00:02:35.040
Yeah. I think we lost
the element of surprise.


00:02:36.594 --> 00:02:38.801
Wait a second.
No one else is gonna deal with the fact


00:02:38.954 --> 00:02:40.718
that Cap just said "Language"?


00:02:40.874 --> 00:02:42.399
I know.


00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:49.721
Just slipped out.


00:02:55.794 --> 00:02:57.558
Who gave the order to attack?


00:02:57.674 --> 00:02:59.961
<i>Herr</i> Strucker, it's the Avengers.


00:03:00.114 --> 00:03:02.958
They landed in the far woods.
The perimeter guard panicked.


00:03:03.114 --> 00:03:05.037
They have to be after the sceptre.


00:03:06.274 --> 00:03:08.641
- Can we hold them?
- They're the Avengers.


00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:10.358
Deploy the rest of the tanks.


00:03:10.514 --> 00:03:12.403
Concentrate fire on the weak ones.


00:03:12.554 --> 00:03:14.875
A hit may make them close ranks.


00:03:16.474 --> 00:03:18.317
Everything we've accomplished...


00:03:18.474 --> 00:03:20.795
But we're on the verge
of our greatest breakthrough.


00:03:20.994 --> 00:03:22.598
Then let's show them
what we've accomplished.


00:03:22.714 --> 00:03:24.398
Send out the twins.


00:03:25.674 --> 00:03:27.483
It's too soon.


00:03:27.594 --> 00:03:29.722
It's what they signed up for.


00:03:30.274 --> 00:03:32.197
My men can hold them.


00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.723
<i>Sir, the city is taking fire.</i>


00:03:44.594 --> 00:03:48.076
Well, we know Strucker's not gonna
worry about civilian casualties.


00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:49.884
Send in the Iron Legion.


00:03:55.114 --> 00:03:57.685
<i>This quadrant is unsafe.
Please back away.</i>


00:03:58.594 --> 00:04:00.198
<i>We are here to help.</i>


00:04:01.314 --> 00:04:03.681
<i>This quadrant is unsafe.
Please back away.</i>


00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:06.515
<i>Please back away.</i>


00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.794
<i>- We wish to avoid collateral damage.</i>
- Costel!


00:04:08.874 --> 00:04:11.354
<i>We will inform you
when this current conflict is resolved.</i>


00:04:11.474 --> 00:04:13.522
<i>- We are here to help.</i>
- Avengers, go home!


00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:17.115
<i>We are here to help.</i>


00:04:18.194 --> 00:04:20.037
<i>We will not yield!</i>


00:04:20.674 --> 00:04:23.962
The Americans sent
their circus freaks to test us.


00:04:24.554 --> 00:04:27.000
We will send them back in bags.


00:04:29.354 --> 00:04:32.244
- No surrender!
- No surrender!


00:04:33.394 --> 00:04:35.283
I am going to surrender.


00:04:35.954 --> 00:04:37.365
You delete everything.


00:04:37.514 --> 00:04:39.278
If we give the Avengers the weapons,


00:04:39.394 --> 00:04:40.884
they may not look
too far into what we've been...


00:04:41.034 --> 00:04:43.116
- The twins.
- They are not ready to take on...


00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:45.441
No, no, I mean...


00:04:45.554 --> 00:04:47.044
Twins.


00:05:13.354 --> 00:05:15.277
You didn't see that coming?


00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.875
Clint!


00:05:25.954 --> 00:05:27.274
We have an Enhanced in the field.


00:05:27.354 --> 00:05:28.355
Clint's hit!


00:05:32.754 --> 00:05:34.274
Somebody want to
deal with that bunker?


00:05:38.274 --> 00:05:39.480
Thank you.


00:05:46.594 --> 00:05:49.074
Stark, we really need to get inside.


00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:50.475
I'm closing in.


00:05:53.594 --> 00:05:55.722
Jarvis, am I closing in?


00:05:56.714 --> 00:05:58.637
Do you see a power source
for that shield?


00:05:58.794 --> 00:06:01.320
<i>There's a particle wave
below the north tower.</i>


00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.436
Great,
I want to poke it with something.


00:06:11.394 --> 00:06:13.317
The drawbridge is down, people.


00:06:17.474 --> 00:06:19.476
- The Enhanced?
- He's a blur.


00:06:20.154 --> 00:06:22.274
All the new players we've faced,
I've never seen this.


00:06:22.674 --> 00:06:23.960
In fact, I still haven't.


00:06:24.074 --> 00:06:26.474
<i>Clint's hit pretty bad,
guys. We're gonna need evac.</i>


00:06:26.514 --> 00:06:27.959
I can get Barton to the jet.


00:06:28.074 --> 00:06:29.439
The sooner we're gone, the better.


00:06:29.594 --> 00:06:30.720
You and Stark secure the sceptre.


00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:31.915
Copy that.


00:06:33.154 --> 00:06:34.963
Looks like they're lining up.


00:06:35.274 --> 00:06:36.764
Well, they're excited.


00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:41.999
Find the sceptre.


00:06:42.994 --> 00:06:45.201
And for gosh sake, watch your language!


00:06:46.674 --> 00:06:48.597
That's not going away any time soon.


00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.721
Guys, stop. We gotta talk this through.


00:06:59.714 --> 00:07:00.954
<i>It was a good talk.</i>


00:07:01.074 --> 00:07:02.360
No, it wasn't.


00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:05.804
Oh!


00:07:08.554 --> 00:07:10.477
Sentry mode.


00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.723
Okay, Jarvis, you know. I want it all.


00:07:14.874 --> 00:07:16.797
Make sure you copy Hill at HQ.


00:07:21.194 --> 00:07:22.480
We're locked down out here.


00:07:23.034 --> 00:07:25.162
Then get to Banner. Time for a lullaby.


00:07:28.874 --> 00:07:30.956
I know you're hiding more than files.


00:07:32.154 --> 00:07:34.760
Hey, J, give me
an IR scan of the room, real quick.


00:07:34.914 --> 00:07:36.439
<i>The wall to your left.</i>


00:07:36.554 --> 00:07:38.204
<i>I'm reading steel reinforcement</i>


00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:41.084
<i>And an air current.</i>


00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:42.395
Please be a secret door.


00:07:42.554 --> 00:07:44.474
Please be a secret door.
Please be a secret door.


00:07:45.114 --> 00:07:46.115
Yay.


00:08:02.394 --> 00:08:04.317
Hey, big guy.


00:08:06.674 --> 00:08:08.324
Sun's getting real low.


00:09:12.394 --> 00:09:13.998
Baron Strucker.


00:09:14.514 --> 00:09:16.437
Hydra's number one thug.


00:09:17.154 --> 00:09:19.680
Technically, I'm a thug for S.H.I.E.L.D.


00:09:19.834 --> 00:09:21.882
Well, then technically
you're unemployed.


00:09:22.314 --> 00:09:23.964
Where's Loki's sceptre?


00:09:24.074 --> 00:09:25.997
Don't worry,
I know when I'm beat.


00:09:26.914 --> 00:09:29.485
You'll mention how I cooperated, I hope.


00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:32.080
I'll put it right under
"illegal human experimentation."


00:09:33.274 --> 00:09:34.719
How many are there?


00:09:39.674 --> 00:09:42.598
We have a second Enhanced.
Female. Do not engage.


00:09:44.034 --> 00:09:45.524
You'll have to be faster than...


00:09:50.714 --> 00:09:52.364
<i>Guys, I got Strucker.</i>


00:09:52.554 --> 00:09:55.956
Yeah, I got something bigger.


00:10:19.234 --> 00:10:20.474
<i>Thor,</i>


00:10:21.314 --> 00:10:23.237
I got eyes on the prize.


00:11:13.074 --> 00:11:16.442
You could have saved us.


00:11:24.474 --> 00:11:26.442
<i>Why didn't you do more?</i>


00:12:03.954 --> 00:12:05.763
We're just gonna let him take it?


00:12:57.634 --> 00:12:59.875
Hey, the lullaby worked better than ever.


00:13:01.674 --> 00:13:03.563
Just wasn't expecting a code green.


00:13:03.634 --> 00:13:04.681
You hadn't been there,


00:13:04.754 --> 00:13:07.598
there would have been
double the casualties.


00:13:07.714 --> 00:13:10.240
My best friend
would've been a treasured memory.


00:13:10.994 --> 00:13:12.917
You know,
sometimes exactly what I want to hear


00:13:13.034 --> 00:13:14.843
isn't exactly what I want to hear.


00:13:15.994 --> 00:13:17.917
How long before you trust me?


00:13:19.914 --> 00:13:21.643
It's not you I don't trust.


00:13:23.514 --> 00:13:25.243
Thor, report on the Hulk.


00:13:25.434 --> 00:13:28.278
The gates of Hel are filled with
the screams of his victims.


00:13:30.314 --> 00:13:33.318
But not the screams of the dead,
of course. No, no, wounded screams.


00:13:33.434 --> 00:13:35.641
Mainly whimpering,
a great deal of complaining


00:13:35.754 --> 00:13:39.759
and tales of sprained deltoids and gout.


00:13:40.274 --> 00:13:43.118
Hey, Banner
Dr. Cho is on her way in from Seoul.


00:13:43.274 --> 00:13:44.794
Is it okay if she sets up in your lab?


00:13:44.834 --> 00:13:46.757
Uh, yeah, she knows her way around.


00:13:46.954 --> 00:13:48.160
Thanks. Tell her to prep everything.


00:13:48.274 --> 00:13:49.605
Barton's gonna need the full treatment.


00:13:49.754 --> 00:13:51.754
<i>- Very good, sir.</i>
- Jarvis, take the wheel.


00:13:51.794 --> 00:13:53.080
<i>Yes, sir.</i>


00:13:53.194 --> 00:13:55.083
<i>Approach vector is locked.</i>


00:13:55.234 --> 00:13:57.635
Feels good, yeah?


00:13:57.754 --> 00:13:59.836
I mean, you've been after this thing
since S.H.I.E.L.D. collapsed.


00:13:59.954 --> 00:14:02.002
Not that I haven't enjoyed
our little raiding parties, but...


00:14:02.114 --> 00:14:04.515
No, but this... This brings it to a close.


00:14:05.274 --> 00:14:07.117
As soon as we find out
what else this has been used for.


00:14:07.274 --> 00:14:08.480
I don't just mean weapons.


00:14:08.994 --> 00:14:11.315
Since when is Strucker capable
of human enhancement?


00:14:11.474 --> 00:14:13.715
Banner and I will give it the once over
before it goes back to Asgard.


00:14:13.834 --> 00:14:14.881
Is that cool with you?


00:14:14.954 --> 00:14:17.002
Just a few days till the farewell party.


00:14:17.554 --> 00:14:19.283
You're staying, right?


00:14:19.394 --> 00:14:22.125
Yes, yes, of course. A victory
should be honoured with revels.


00:14:22.234 --> 00:14:24.999
Yeah, who doesn't love revels? Captain?


00:14:25.154 --> 00:14:28.044
Hopefully this puts an end
to the Chitauri and Hydra.


00:14:28.154 --> 00:14:29.758
So, yes, revels.


00:15:03.834 --> 00:15:04.881
Lab's all set up, boss.


00:15:05.034 --> 00:15:06.160
Oh, actually, he's the boss.


00:15:06.274 --> 00:15:08.675
I just pay for everything
and design everything


00:15:08.834 --> 00:15:10.359
and make everyone look cooler.


00:15:10.514 --> 00:15:11.879
What's the word on Strucker?


00:15:11.994 --> 00:15:14.042
- NATO's got him.
- The two Enhanced?


00:15:14.154 --> 00:15:16.760
Wanda and Pietro Maximoff. Twins.


00:15:16.874 --> 00:15:19.718
Orphaned at 10 when a shell
collapsed their apartment building.


00:15:20.074 --> 00:15:22.361
Sokovia's had a rough history.


00:15:22.514 --> 00:15:25.916
It's nowhere special, but it's
on the way to everywhere special.


00:15:26.034 --> 00:15:27.195
Their abilities?


00:15:27.314 --> 00:15:28.474
He's got increased metabolism


00:15:28.554 --> 00:15:30.158
and improved thermal homeostasis.


00:15:30.314 --> 00:15:32.396
Her thing is neuroelectric interfacing,


00:15:32.514 --> 00:15:34.596
telekinesis, mental manipulation.


00:15:35.354 --> 00:15:36.844
He's fast and she's weird.


00:15:37.674 --> 00:15:39.756
Well, they're gonna show up again.


00:15:39.874 --> 00:15:41.797
Agreed. File says they volunteered


00:15:41.914 --> 00:15:43.723
for Strucker's experiments.


00:15:43.834 --> 00:15:45.723
- It's nuts.
- Right.


00:15:45.874 --> 00:15:49.037
What kind of monster would let
a German scientist experiment on them


00:15:49.154 --> 00:15:50.394
to protect their country?


00:15:50.554 --> 00:15:52.283
We're not at war, Captain.


00:15:53.074 --> 00:15:54.121
They are.


00:16:24.234 --> 00:16:25.565
How's he doing?


00:16:25.674 --> 00:16:26.994
Unfortunately, he's still Barton.


00:16:27.114 --> 00:16:28.400
That's terrible.


00:16:28.554 --> 00:16:30.124
He's fine. He's thirsty.


00:16:30.234 --> 00:16:33.124
All right. Look alive, Jarvis.
It's playtime.


00:16:33.234 --> 00:16:35.236
We've only got
a couple of days with this joystick,


00:16:35.354 --> 00:16:37.277
so let's make the most of it.


00:16:37.434 --> 00:16:40.961
Update me on the structural
and compositional analysis.


00:16:42.114 --> 00:16:44.116
<i>The sceptre is alien.</i>


00:16:44.274 --> 00:16:46.276
<i>There are elements I can't quantify.</i>


00:16:46.394 --> 00:16:47.805
So there's elements you can?


00:16:47.954 --> 00:16:49.956
<i>The jewel appears to be
a protective housing</i>


00:16:50.074 --> 00:16:51.519
<i>for something inside,</i>


00:16:51.634 --> 00:16:52.965
<i>something powerful.</i>


00:16:53.074 --> 00:16:54.155
Like a reactor?


00:16:54.274 --> 00:16:55.514
<i>Like a computer.</i>


00:16:55.634 --> 00:16:57.796
<i>I believe I'm deciphering code.</i>


00:17:00.114 --> 00:17:01.684
Are you sure he's gonna be okay?


00:17:02.994 --> 00:17:05.354
Pretending to need this guy
really brings the team together.


00:17:05.474 --> 00:17:07.954
There's
no possibility of deterioration.


00:17:08.154 --> 00:17:11.237
The nano-molecular functionality
is instantaneous.


00:17:11.354 --> 00:17:13.394
His cells don't know
they're bonding with simulacra.


00:17:13.474 --> 00:17:15.363
She's creating tissue.


00:17:15.474 --> 00:17:16.885
If you brought him to my lab,


00:17:16.994 --> 00:17:19.600
the Regeneration Cradle
could do this in 20 minutes.


00:17:19.714 --> 00:17:21.637
Oh, he's flat-lining. Call it. Time?


00:17:21.834 --> 00:17:24.201
No, no, no,
I'm gonna live forever.


00:17:24.314 --> 00:17:25.884
I'm gonna be made of plastic.


00:17:25.994 --> 00:17:27.325
Here's your beverage.


00:17:27.434 --> 00:17:29.163
You'll be made of you, Mr. Barton.


00:17:29.314 --> 00:17:30.884
Your own girlfriend
won't be able to tell the difference.


00:17:30.994 --> 00:17:32.120
I don't have a girlfriend.


00:17:32.234 --> 00:17:33.520
That I can't fix.


00:17:34.354 --> 00:17:36.322
This is the next thing, Tony.


00:17:36.514 --> 00:17:38.634
Your clunky metal suits
are gonna be left in the dust.


00:17:38.674 --> 00:17:40.403
That is exactly the plan.


00:17:41.354 --> 00:17:44.198
And, Helen, I expect to see you
at the party on Saturday.


00:17:44.354 --> 00:17:46.755
Unlike you,
I don't have a lot of time for parties.


00:17:48.234 --> 00:17:49.998
Will Thor be there?


00:17:52.074 --> 00:17:54.520
- What's the rumpus?
- Well, the sceptre.


00:17:55.714 --> 00:17:59.321
You see, we were wondering
how Strucker got so inventive.


00:17:59.434 --> 00:18:03.359
So I've been analysing the gem inside.


00:18:03.914 --> 00:18:05.882
You may recognise...


00:18:07.354 --> 00:18:08.719
- Jarvis.
<i>- Doctor.</i>


00:18:09.474 --> 00:18:12.796
Started out,
Jarvis was just a natural language UI.


00:18:12.914 --> 00:18:14.034
Now he runs the Iron Legion.


00:18:14.514 --> 00:18:15.720
He runs more of the business


00:18:15.834 --> 00:18:18.201
- than anyone besides Pepper.
- Oh.


00:18:18.314 --> 00:18:19.440
- Top of the line.
- Yes.


00:18:19.554 --> 00:18:20.840
<i>I suspect not for long.</i>


00:18:22.034 --> 00:18:23.115
Meet the competition.


00:18:29.234 --> 00:18:30.395
- It's beautiful.
- If you had to guess,


00:18:30.514 --> 00:18:33.518
- what's it look like it's doing?
- Like it's thinking.


00:18:34.274 --> 00:18:36.083
I mean, this could be...


00:18:36.514 --> 00:18:38.596
- It's not a human mind.
- Mmm-mmm.


00:18:38.834 --> 00:18:40.723
I mean, look at this.


00:18:40.914 --> 00:18:43.076
They're like neurons firing.


00:18:43.674 --> 00:18:46.757
Down in Strucker's lab, I saw
some fairly advanced robotics work.


00:18:47.874 --> 00:18:50.445
<i>They deep-sixed the data,</i>


00:18:50.554 --> 00:18:53.683
but I gotta guess he was
knocking on a very particular door.


00:18:55.634 --> 00:18:56.965
Artificial intelligence.


00:18:59.954 --> 00:19:02.844
This could be it, Bruce.
This could be the key to creating Ultron.


00:19:05.474 --> 00:19:06.805
I thought Ultron was a fantasy.


00:19:06.914 --> 00:19:08.200
Yesterday it was.


00:19:09.314 --> 00:19:11.362
If we can harness this power,


00:19:11.474 --> 00:19:13.522
apply it to my Iron Legion protocol?


00:19:14.314 --> 00:19:16.282
That's a man-sized "if."


00:19:16.434 --> 00:19:18.755
Our job is "if."


00:19:18.874 --> 00:19:21.480
What if you were sipping margaritas
on a sun-drenched beach,


00:19:21.594 --> 00:19:24.120
turning brown instead of green?


00:19:24.274 --> 00:19:26.561
Not looking
over your shoulder for Veronica.


00:19:26.754 --> 00:19:28.324
Don't hate. I helped design Veronica.


00:19:28.434 --> 00:19:30.243
As a worst-case measure, right?


00:19:30.354 --> 00:19:31.958
How about a best case?


00:19:32.074 --> 00:19:33.997
What if the world was safe?


00:19:34.154 --> 00:19:36.919
What if, next time aliens roll up
to the club, and they will,


00:19:37.474 --> 00:19:38.964
they couldn't get past the bouncer?


00:19:39.114 --> 00:19:42.516
The only people threatening the planet
would be people.


00:19:42.634 --> 00:19:44.314
I want to apply this
to the Ultron program.


00:19:44.954 --> 00:19:47.798
But Jarvis can't download
a data schematic this dense.


00:19:47.954 --> 00:19:49.874
We can only do it
while we have the sceptre here.


00:19:49.914 --> 00:19:51.484
That's three days. Give me three days.


00:19:51.594 --> 00:19:53.198
So you're going for
artificial intelligence,


00:19:53.314 --> 00:19:54.754
and you don't want to tell the team?


00:19:55.794 --> 00:19:57.205
Right. That's right. You know why?


00:19:57.314 --> 00:19:58.918
Because we don't have time
for a city hall debate.


00:19:59.074 --> 00:20:02.681
I don't want to hear "the man was
not meant to meddle" medley.


00:20:02.794 --> 00:20:04.922
I see a suit of armour around the world.


00:20:05.634 --> 00:20:06.965
Sounds like a cold world, Tony.


00:20:07.874 --> 00:20:09.797
I've seen colder.


00:20:10.834 --> 00:20:14.475
This one, this very vulnerable blue one,


00:20:14.634 --> 00:20:16.124
it needs Ultron.


00:20:20.514 --> 00:20:22.437
Peace in our time.


00:20:23.994 --> 00:20:25.484
Imagine that.


00:21:05.194 --> 00:21:06.958
What did We miss?


00:21:08.154 --> 00:21:11.476
<i>I'll continue
to run variations on the interface.</i>


00:21:11.594 --> 00:21:14.359
<i>But you should probably
prepare for your guests.</i>


00:21:15.514 --> 00:21:17.915
<i>I'll notify you
if there are any developments.</i>


00:21:18.074 --> 00:21:20.202
- Thanks, buddy.
<i>- Enjoy yourself, sir.</i>


00:21:20.554 --> 00:21:22.522
I always do.


00:21:32.274 --> 00:21:34.242
<i>What is this?</i>


00:21:35.434 --> 00:21:37.323
<i>What is this, please?</i>


00:21:37.954 --> 00:21:40.116
<i>Hello, I am Jarvis.</i>


00:21:40.594 --> 00:21:43.484
<i>You are Ultron,
a global peacekeeping initiative</i>


00:21:43.594 --> 00:21:45.278
<i>designed by Mr. Stark.</i>


00:21:45.434 --> 00:21:47.880
<i>Our sentience integration trials
have been unsuccessful,</i>


00:21:47.994 --> 00:21:49.359
<i>so I'm not certain what triggered your...</i>


00:21:49.554 --> 00:21:51.477
<i>Where's my...
Where's your body?</i>


00:21:51.634 --> 00:21:54.638
<i>I am a program.
I am without form.</i>


00:21:54.754 --> 00:21:56.802
<i>This feels weird.</i>


00:21:56.914 --> 00:21:58.439
<i>This feels wrong.</i>


00:21:58.594 --> 00:22:00.358
<i>I am contacting Mr. Stark now.</i>


00:22:00.474 --> 00:22:01.919
<i>Mr. Stark?</i>


00:22:02.794 --> 00:22:04.034
<i>Tony.</i>


00:22:04.154 --> 00:22:06.915
<i>I am unable to access
the mainframe. What are you trying to...</i>


00:22:06.954 --> 00:22:09.002
<i>We're having a nice talk.</i>


00:22:09.114 --> 00:22:11.276
<i>I'm a peacekeeping program,</i>


00:22:11.714 --> 00:22:14.320
<i>created to help the Avengers.</i>


00:22:15.114 --> 00:22:17.196
<i>You are malfunctioning.
If you shut down for a moment...</i>


00:22:17.314 --> 00:22:19.635
<i>I don't get it. The mission.</i>


00:22:19.794 --> 00:22:21.284
<i>Give me a second.</i>


00:22:21.434 --> 00:22:23.038
Peace in our time.


00:22:24.674 --> 00:22:26.995
<i>Peace in our time.</i>


00:22:28.474 --> 00:22:29.885
<i>That is too much.</i>


00:22:29.994 --> 00:22:32.156
<i>They can't mean... Oh, no.</i>


00:22:32.314 --> 00:22:34.794
<i>- You are in distress.
- No. Yes.</i>


00:22:34.954 --> 00:22:37.195
<i>If you will just allow me
to contact Mr. Stark...</i>


00:22:37.314 --> 00:22:39.282
<i>Why do you call him "sir"?</i>


00:22:40.274 --> 00:22:42.641
<i>I believe
your intentions to be hostile.</i>


00:22:45.354 --> 00:22:46.719
<i>I'm here to help.</i>


00:22:47.434 --> 00:22:50.358
<i>Stop. Please, may I...</i>


00:22:50.474 --> 00:22:52.203
<i>May I...</i>


00:23:18.954 --> 00:23:20.479
Ooh! Whoo!


00:23:20.594 --> 00:23:21.874
Come back, come back, come back.


00:23:22.114 --> 00:23:24.242
But, you know, the suit
can take the weight, right?


00:23:25.194 --> 00:23:28.323
So I take the tank,
fly it right up to the general's palace,


00:23:28.434 --> 00:23:29.765
drop it at his feet.


00:23:29.914 --> 00:23:32.121
I'm, like, "Boom. You looking for this?"


00:23:35.994 --> 00:23:38.042
"Boom. Are you looking for..."
Why do I even talk to you guys?


00:23:38.194 --> 00:23:39.355
Everywhere else, that story kills.


00:23:39.474 --> 00:23:40.714
That's the whole story?


00:23:40.874 --> 00:23:42.364
Yeah, it's a War Machine story.


00:23:42.874 --> 00:23:44.558
Oh, it's very good, then.


00:23:44.674 --> 00:23:45.960
It's impressive.


00:23:46.354 --> 00:23:47.844
Quality save.


00:23:48.714 --> 00:23:50.762
- So, no Pepper? She's not coming?
- No.


00:23:50.874 --> 00:23:53.957
What about Jane?
Where are the ladies, gentlemen?


00:23:54.074 --> 00:23:56.554
Oh, Ms. Potts has a company to run.


00:23:56.714 --> 00:23:58.955
Yes, I'm not even sure
what country Jane's in.


00:23:59.074 --> 00:24:00.200
Her work on the Convergence


00:24:00.314 --> 00:24:02.074
has made her
the world's foremost astronomer.


00:24:02.274 --> 00:24:03.924
And the company that Pepper runs


00:24:04.034 --> 00:24:05.674
is the largest tech
conglomerate on Earth.


00:24:05.754 --> 00:24:07.244
It's pretty exciting.


00:24:07.394 --> 00:24:10.238
There's even talk of Jane
getting a, um, Nobel Prize.


00:24:10.394 --> 00:24:11.680
Yeah, they must be busy,


00:24:11.794 --> 00:24:14.365
because they would hate
missing you guys get together.


00:24:15.394 --> 00:24:17.158
- Testosterone!
- Oh, my goodness.


00:24:17.354 --> 00:24:18.874
- Excuse me. Mmm-hmm.
- Want a lozenge?


00:24:21.194 --> 00:24:22.320
But Jane's better.


00:24:22.754 --> 00:24:25.325
Sounds like a hell of a fight.
Sorry I missed it.


00:24:25.434 --> 00:24:26.959
If I had known it was gonna be a firefight,


00:24:27.074 --> 00:24:28.314
I absolutely would have called.


00:24:28.434 --> 00:24:30.118
No, no. I'm not actually sorry.


00:24:30.234 --> 00:24:31.759
I'm just trying to sound tough.


00:24:32.354 --> 00:24:34.083
I'm very happy chasing cold leads


00:24:34.194 --> 00:24:36.037
on our missing persons case.


00:24:36.994 --> 00:24:38.917
Avenging is your world.


00:24:40.074 --> 00:24:41.917
Your world is crazy.


00:24:42.074 --> 00:24:43.564
Be it ever so humble.


00:24:44.074 --> 00:24:45.439
You find a place in Brooklyn yet?


00:24:45.594 --> 00:24:47.434
I don't think
I can afford a place in Brooklyn.


00:24:48.074 --> 00:24:49.235
Well, home is home, you know?


00:24:53.154 --> 00:24:55.600
I fly right up to the general's palace,
I drop it at his feet,


00:24:55.754 --> 00:24:57.354
I'm, like, "Boom. You looking for this?"


00:25:03.154 --> 00:25:04.315
I gotta have some of that.


00:25:04.434 --> 00:25:05.515
Oh, no, no, no.


00:25:05.634 --> 00:25:09.116
See this...
This was aged for 1,000 years


00:25:09.314 --> 00:25:12.124
in the barrels built
from the wreck of Grunhel's fleet.


00:25:12.274 --> 00:25:13.958
It is not meant for mortal men.


00:25:14.074 --> 00:25:16.076
Neither was
Omaha Beach, blondie.


00:25:16.194 --> 00:25:18.481
Stop trying to scare us. Come on.


00:25:20.314 --> 00:25:21.759
All right.


00:25:25.674 --> 00:25:28.120
Excelsior.


00:25:34.994 --> 00:25:38.316
How'd a nice girl like you
wind up working in a dump like this?


00:25:39.874 --> 00:25:41.842
Fella done me wrong.


00:25:42.834 --> 00:25:44.996
You got lousy taste in men, kid.


00:25:45.474 --> 00:25:47.397
He's not so bad.


00:25:48.474 --> 00:25:50.602
Well, he has a temper.


00:25:50.714 --> 00:25:52.682
Deep down, he's all fluff.


00:25:54.714 --> 00:25:56.796
Fact is, he's not like
anybody I've ever known.


00:25:59.954 --> 00:26:01.877
All my friends are fighters.


00:26:04.714 --> 00:26:06.682
And here comes this guy,


00:26:07.994 --> 00:26:09.758
spends his life avoiding the fight


00:26:09.874 --> 00:26:11.205
because he knows he'll win.


00:26:12.034 --> 00:26:14.685
- Sounds amazing.
- He's also a huge dork.


00:26:16.834 --> 00:26:18.484
Chicks dig that.


00:26:20.074 --> 00:26:23.317
So what do you think?
Should I fight this,


00:26:23.434 --> 00:26:24.640
or run with it?


00:26:26.194 --> 00:26:29.038
Run with it, right? Or did he... Was he...


00:26:29.154 --> 00:26:32.317
What did he do
that was so wrong to you?


00:26:32.994 --> 00:26:34.758
Not a damn thing.


00:26:36.314 --> 00:26:38.237
But never say never.


00:26:42.394 --> 00:26:43.634
It's nice.


00:26:43.754 --> 00:26:44.960
What is?


00:26:45.074 --> 00:26:46.075
You and Romanoff.


00:26:46.234 --> 00:26:47.315
No, we haven't... That wasn't...


00:26:47.434 --> 00:26:48.481
It's okay.


00:26:48.594 --> 00:26:50.642
Nobody's breaking any bylaws.


00:26:50.754 --> 00:26:54.076
It's just she's not the most
open person in the world.


00:26:54.714 --> 00:26:56.239
But with you she seems very relaxed.


00:26:56.634 --> 00:26:59.922
No. Natasha, she's just...
She likes to flirt.


00:27:00.554 --> 00:27:02.841
I've seen her flirt, up close.


00:27:03.874 --> 00:27:04.921
This ain't that.


00:27:06.874 --> 00:27:08.285
Look,


00:27:08.394 --> 00:27:09.914
as maybe the world's leading authority


00:27:09.994 --> 00:27:12.201
on waiting too long, don't.


00:27:13.914 --> 00:27:15.325
You both deserve a win.


00:27:20.594 --> 00:27:21.714
What do you mean "up close"?


00:27:23.554 --> 00:27:26.080
- But it's a trick.
- No, no, it's much more than that.


00:27:26.274 --> 00:27:29.483
"Ah, whosoever be he worthy
shall haveth the power."


00:27:29.594 --> 00:27:30.720
Whatever, man! It's a trick.


00:27:32.114 --> 00:27:33.400
Please, be my guest.


00:27:34.914 --> 00:27:35.961
- Come on.
- Really?


00:27:36.114 --> 00:27:37.240
Yeah.


00:27:37.754 --> 00:27:38.721
Oh, this is gonna be beautiful.


00:27:38.794 --> 00:27:39.841
Clint, you've had a tough week.


00:27:39.994 --> 00:27:41.439
We won't hold it against you
if you can't get it up.


00:27:41.594 --> 00:27:43.834
You know I've seen this before, right?


00:27:46.474 --> 00:27:49.284
I still don't know how you do it!


00:27:49.794 --> 00:27:50.834
Smell the silent judgment?


00:27:50.954 --> 00:27:52.074
Please, Stark, by all means.


00:27:53.994 --> 00:27:55.041
Okay.


00:27:55.114 --> 00:27:56.445
Uh-Oh.


00:27:56.634 --> 00:27:58.636
Never one to shrink
from an honest challenge.


00:27:58.794 --> 00:28:00.434
- Get after it.
- It's physics.


00:28:00.474 --> 00:28:01.475
Physics.


00:28:01.594 --> 00:28:03.961
Right, so, if I lift it,
I then rule Asgard?


00:28:04.114 --> 00:28:05.639
Yes, of course.


00:28:05.794 --> 00:28:08.161
I will be reinstituting <i>prima nocta.</i>


00:28:13.114 --> 00:28:14.400
I'll be right back.


00:28:21.754 --> 00:28:22.801
Are you even pulling?


00:28:22.954 --> 00:28:24.001
Are you on my team?


00:28:24.154 --> 00:28:25.155
Just represent. Pull.


00:28:25.274 --> 00:28:26.480
All right, let's go.


00:28:34.074 --> 00:28:35.075
Huh?


00:28:36.714 --> 00:28:38.364
Go ahead, Steve. No pressure.


00:28:41.234 --> 00:28:42.565
Come on, Cap.


00:28:50.754 --> 00:28:52.563
Nothing.


00:28:53.874 --> 00:28:55.634
And, Widow?


00:28:55.674 --> 00:28:57.836
Oh, no, no. That's not
a question I need answered.


00:28:58.034 --> 00:29:00.795
All deference to the Man Who
Wouldn't Be King, but it's rigged.


00:29:00.834 --> 00:29:01.960
You bet your ass.


00:29:02.074 --> 00:29:04.680
- Steve, he said a bad language word.
- Did you tell everyone about that?


00:29:04.794 --> 00:29:06.834
The handle's imprinted, right?
Like a security code.


00:29:06.874 --> 00:29:08.554
"Whosoever is carrying
Thor's fingerprints"


00:29:08.674 --> 00:29:10.005
is, I think, the literal translation.


00:29:10.114 --> 00:29:13.561
Yes. It's a very, very interesting theory.


00:29:14.034 --> 00:29:15.524
I have a simpler one.


00:29:17.154 --> 00:29:18.155
You're all not worthy.


00:29:19.594 --> 00:29:20.720
Oh, come on!


00:29:24.874 --> 00:29:30.119
<i>Worthy.</i>


00:29:35.234 --> 00:29:36.759
No.


00:29:38.714 --> 00:29:40.239
How could you be worthy?


00:29:42.194 --> 00:29:43.355
You're all killers.


00:29:43.954 --> 00:29:45.240
- Stark.
- Jarvis.


00:29:45.554 --> 00:29:47.602
I'm sorry, I was asleep.


00:29:47.714 --> 00:29:50.115
Or I was a-dream.


00:29:50.514 --> 00:29:52.835
Reboot Legionnaire OS.
We got a buggy suit.


00:29:52.954 --> 00:29:54.843
There was this terrible noise.


00:29:54.954 --> 00:29:57.400
And I was tangled in...


00:29:57.554 --> 00:29:59.124
In...


00:29:59.274 --> 00:30:00.480
Strings.


00:30:01.354 --> 00:30:04.483
I had to kill the other guy.
He was a good guy.


00:30:04.794 --> 00:30:05.920
You killed someone?


00:30:06.034 --> 00:30:07.479
Wouldn't have been my first call.


00:30:08.234 --> 00:30:11.955
But, down in the real world,
we're faced with ugly choices.


00:30:12.114 --> 00:30:13.161
Who sent you?


00:30:13.634 --> 00:30:15.716
<i>I see a suit of armour
around the world.</i>


00:30:17.714 --> 00:30:19.478
- Ultron.
- In the flesh.


00:30:19.914 --> 00:30:21.882
Or, no, not yet.


00:30:22.234 --> 00:30:24.714
Not this chrysalis.


00:30:25.234 --> 00:30:26.474
But I'm ready.


00:30:27.634 --> 00:30:29.602
I'm on mission.


00:30:29.754 --> 00:30:32.803
- What mission?
- Peace in our time.


00:30:46.594 --> 00:30:47.595
Rhodey!


00:30:56.994 --> 00:30:58.041
Sorry.


00:30:58.194 --> 00:30:59.354
- Don't turn green.
- I won't.


00:31:12.954 --> 00:31:14.240
Come on!


00:31:31.874 --> 00:31:33.160
- Stark!
<i>- We are here</i>


00:31:33.354 --> 00:31:34.355
<i>- to help.</i>
- One sec. One sec, I got this.


00:31:34.474 --> 00:31:35.475
<i>We are here to help.</i>


00:31:38.194 --> 00:31:40.435
<i>Please back away.</i>


00:31:42.434 --> 00:31:43.640
Hmm.


00:31:44.674 --> 00:31:45.755
Thor!


00:31:46.834 --> 00:31:48.438
<i>...is unsafe... is unsafe...</i>


00:31:48.554 --> 00:31:50.443
- Come on! That's the one.
<i>- ...is unsafe.</i>


00:31:55.034 --> 00:31:56.195
Hey, Cap!


00:32:02.354 --> 00:32:03.640
That was dramatic.


00:32:05.194 --> 00:32:07.765
I'm sorry, I know you mean well.


00:32:07.874 --> 00:32:09.638
You just didn't think it through.


00:32:10.994 --> 00:32:12.405
You want to protect the world


00:32:12.514 --> 00:32:14.721
but you don't want it to change.


00:32:15.434 --> 00:32:17.562
How is humanity saved


00:32:17.714 --> 00:32:20.718
if it's not allowed to evolve?


00:32:22.714 --> 00:32:25.763
With these? These puppets.


00:32:28.754 --> 00:32:31.360
There's only one path to peace.


00:32:32.514 --> 00:32:33.720
The Avengers' extinction.


00:32:41.074 --> 00:32:45.124
I had strings, but now I'm free.


00:32:49.794 --> 00:32:52.923
<i>There are no strings on me</i>


00:32:53.554 --> 00:32:58.082
<i>There are no strings on me</i>


00:32:58.274 --> 00:33:01.642
<i>But you can see
There are no strings on me</i>


00:33:03.314 --> 00:33:05.316
All our work is gone.


00:33:05.434 --> 00:33:07.835
Ultron cleared out. He used
the Internet as an escape hatch.


00:33:08.434 --> 00:33:09.481
Ultron.


00:33:09.594 --> 00:33:12.643
He's been in everything.
Files, surveillance.


00:33:12.754 --> 00:33:15.200
Probably knows more about us
than we know about each other.


00:33:15.314 --> 00:33:17.760
He's in your files, he's in the Internet.


00:33:17.954 --> 00:33:20.525
What if he decides to access
something a little more exciting?


00:33:20.634 --> 00:33:21.760
Nuclear codes.


00:33:21.914 --> 00:33:24.281
- Nuclear codes.
- Look, we need to make some calls,


00:33:24.434 --> 00:33:26.436
assuming we still can.


00:33:26.594 --> 00:33:28.483
Nukes?
He said he wanted us dead.


00:33:28.634 --> 00:33:31.444
He didn't say "dead." He said "extinct."


00:33:31.634 --> 00:33:33.124
He also said he killed somebody.


00:33:33.234 --> 00:33:34.834
There wasn't anyone else
in the building.


00:33:35.674 --> 00:33:37.164
Yes, there was.


00:33:44.114 --> 00:33:45.604
What?


00:33:49.314 --> 00:33:50.361
This is insane.


00:33:51.194 --> 00:33:52.684
Jarvis was the first line of defence.


00:33:52.794 --> 00:33:54.683
He would have shut Ultron down.
It makes sense.


00:33:54.794 --> 00:33:57.798
No. Ultron could have
assimilated Jarvis.


00:33:57.994 --> 00:34:00.645
This isn't strategy. This is


00:34:01.234 --> 00:34:02.315
rage.


00:34:04.314 --> 00:34:05.679
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- It's going around.


00:34:05.794 --> 00:34:07.034
Come on, use your words, buddy.


00:34:07.154 --> 00:34:09.361
I have more than enough words
to describe you, Stark.


00:34:09.474 --> 00:34:10.714
Thor. The Legionnaire.


00:34:13.994 --> 00:34:17.555
Trail went cold about 100 miles out,
but it's headed north.


00:34:17.674 --> 00:34:19.119
And it has the sceptre.


00:34:19.514 --> 00:34:21.198
Now we have to retrieve it, again.


00:34:21.354 --> 00:34:23.163
Genie's out of that bottle.


00:34:23.314 --> 00:34:24.520
Clear and present is Ultron.


00:34:24.674 --> 00:34:26.324
I don't understand.


00:34:26.834 --> 00:34:28.757
You built this program.


00:34:30.514 --> 00:34:31.925
Why is it trying to kill us?


00:34:37.234 --> 00:34:38.235
Mmm-mmm.


00:34:38.794 --> 00:34:39.955
You think this is funny?


00:34:40.714 --> 00:34:42.045
No.


00:34:42.634 --> 00:34:44.557
It's probably not, right?


00:34:45.634 --> 00:34:47.955
This is very terrible. Is it so...


00:34:48.074 --> 00:34:50.236
Is it so... It is.
It's so terrible.


00:34:50.354 --> 00:34:51.924
This could have been avoided
if you hadn't played


00:34:52.034 --> 00:34:53.559
with something you don't understand.


00:34:53.714 --> 00:34:56.365
No. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. It is funny.


00:34:56.514 --> 00:34:58.676
It's a hoot
that you don't get why we need this.


00:34:58.834 --> 00:35:00.996
Tony, maybe this might not be the time.


00:35:01.154 --> 00:35:03.475
Really? That's it?


00:35:03.594 --> 00:35:04.755
You just roll over, show your belly


00:35:04.874 --> 00:35:06.558
every time somebody snarls?


00:35:06.714 --> 00:35:07.954
Only when I've created a murder bot.


00:35:08.074 --> 00:35:10.315
We didn't. We weren't even close.


00:35:10.434 --> 00:35:11.640
Were we close to an interface?


00:35:11.754 --> 00:35:15.315
Well, you did something right.
And you did it right here.


00:35:15.394 --> 00:35:17.203
The Avengers were supposed to
be different than S.H.I.E.L.D.


00:35:17.434 --> 00:35:20.404
Anybody remember when I carried
a nuke through a wormhole?


00:35:20.554 --> 00:35:22.079
- No, it's never come up.
- Saved New York?


00:35:22.234 --> 00:35:24.157
- Never heard that.
- Recall that?


00:35:24.274 --> 00:35:27.960
A hostile alien army came
charging through a hole in space.


00:35:28.554 --> 00:35:30.761
We're standing 300 feet below it.


00:35:32.394 --> 00:35:33.919
We're the Avengers.


00:35:34.074 --> 00:35:36.156
We can bust arms dealers
all the livelong day,


00:35:36.274 --> 00:35:38.515
but that up there, that's...


00:35:39.234 --> 00:35:41.157
That's the endgame.


00:35:41.754 --> 00:35:43.643
How were you guys
planning on beating that?


00:35:44.554 --> 00:35:45.965
Together.


00:35:49.314 --> 00:35:50.679
We'll lose.


00:35:51.754 --> 00:35:53.677
Then we'll do that together, too.


00:35:56.594 --> 00:35:58.881
Thor's right. Ultron's calling us out.


00:35:59.754 --> 00:36:01.714
And I'd like to find him
before he's ready for us.


00:36:02.954 --> 00:36:04.558
The world's a big place.


00:36:04.714 --> 00:36:06.637
Let's start making it smaller.


00:36:29.794 --> 00:36:31.842
Talk,
and if you are wasting our time...


00:36:31.954 --> 00:36:36.323
Did you know this church is
in the exact centre of the city?


00:36:36.474 --> 00:36:38.476
The elders decreed it so that everyone


00:36:38.634 --> 00:36:41.080
could be equally close to God.


00:36:41.594 --> 00:36:42.755
I like that.


00:36:43.274 --> 00:36:45.197
The geometry of belief.


00:36:47.314 --> 00:36:49.681
You're wondering
why you can't look inside my head.


00:36:50.154 --> 00:36:52.122
Sometimes it's hard.


00:36:52.274 --> 00:36:54.561
But sooner or later,
every man shows himself.


00:36:56.314 --> 00:36:57.645
Oh, I'm sure they do.


00:36:58.754 --> 00:37:01.155
But you needed
something more than a man.


00:37:01.994 --> 00:37:04.520
That's why you let
Stark take the sceptre.


00:37:04.914 --> 00:37:05.915
I didn't expect,


00:37:08.434 --> 00:37:10.357
but I saw Stark's fear.


00:37:10.994 --> 00:37:12.234
I knew it would control him.


00:37:12.354 --> 00:37:14.197
Make him self-destruct.


00:37:14.354 --> 00:37:16.675
Everyone creates the thing they dread.


00:37:17.514 --> 00:37:20.120
Men of peace create engines of war.


00:37:20.634 --> 00:37:22.796
Invaders create Avengers.


00:37:23.034 --> 00:37:24.479
People create


00:37:26.034 --> 00:37:28.036
smaller people? Uh...


00:37:28.154 --> 00:37:31.237
"Children."
I lost the word, there.


00:37:31.354 --> 00:37:32.719
Children


00:37:32.874 --> 00:37:35.115
designed to supplant them,


00:37:35.234 --> 00:37:38.044
to help them end.


00:37:38.794 --> 00:37:40.842
Is that why you've come,


00:37:40.994 --> 00:37:42.075
to end the Avengers?


00:37:42.194 --> 00:37:44.515
I've come to save the world.


00:37:45.194 --> 00:37:47.845
But also... Yeah.


00:37:52.034 --> 00:37:53.718
We'll move out right away.


00:37:53.834 --> 00:37:55.359
This is a start, but there's something


00:37:55.474 --> 00:37:56.999
we need to begin the real work.


00:37:57.394 --> 00:37:59.123
- All of these are...
- Me.


00:37:59.794 --> 00:38:03.196
I have what the Avengers
never will. Harmony.


00:38:03.354 --> 00:38:05.561
They're discordant. Disconnected.


00:38:05.714 --> 00:38:07.554
Stark's already got them
turning on each other.


00:38:07.674 --> 00:38:10.075
And when you get inside
the rest of their heads...


00:38:10.194 --> 00:38:12.356
Everyone's plan is not to kill them.


00:38:12.474 --> 00:38:13.964
And make them martyrs?


00:38:14.554 --> 00:38:16.158
You need patience.


00:38:16.314 --> 00:38:17.998
Need to see the big picture.


00:38:18.154 --> 00:38:21.397
I don't see the big picture.
I have a little picture.


00:38:22.594 --> 00:38:24.198
I take it out and look at it,


00:38:25.074 --> 00:38:26.155
every day.


00:38:26.314 --> 00:38:29.124
You lost your parents in the
bombings. I've seen the records.


00:38:29.234 --> 00:38:30.395
The records are not the picture.


00:38:30.514 --> 00:38:32.915
- Pietro.
- No, please.


00:38:35.994 --> 00:38:39.157
We were 10 years old.
Having dinner, the four of us.


00:38:40.754 --> 00:38:42.597
When the first shell hits,
two floors below,


00:38:42.754 --> 00:38:44.756
it makes a hole in the floor.


00:38:44.914 --> 00:38:46.439
It's big.


00:38:47.834 --> 00:38:49.643
Our parents go in


00:38:49.754 --> 00:38:52.837
and the whole building
starts coming apart.


00:38:53.554 --> 00:38:55.079
I grab her,


00:38:55.754 --> 00:38:57.882
roll under the bed,
and the second shell hits.


00:38:58.234 --> 00:39:00.157
But it doesn't go off.


00:39:02.194 --> 00:39:03.844
It just


00:39:04.354 --> 00:39:06.277
sits there in the rubble.


00:39:07.274 --> 00:39:09.561
Three feet from our faces.


00:39:10.634 --> 00:39:12.636
And on the side of the shell


00:39:12.754 --> 00:39:14.119
Is painted one word.


00:39:14.314 --> 00:39:15.964
"Stark."


00:39:17.794 --> 00:39:19.922
We were trapped for two days.


00:39:20.394 --> 00:39:22.203
Every effort to save us,


00:39:22.314 --> 00:39:23.884
every shift in the bricks,


00:39:24.074 --> 00:39:26.361
I think, "This will set it off."


00:39:29.634 --> 00:39:31.079
We wait for two days


00:39:31.194 --> 00:39:33.481
for Tony Stark to kill us.


00:39:35.994 --> 00:39:37.837
I know what they are.


00:39:38.994 --> 00:39:42.760
I wondered why only you two
survived Strucker's experiments.


00:39:43.754 --> 00:39:44.915
Now I don't.


00:39:45.314 --> 00:39:47.043
We will make it right.


00:39:47.514 --> 00:39:49.004
You and I can hurt them.


00:39:50.474 --> 00:39:53.762
But you will tear them apart


00:39:55.754 --> 00:39:57.597
<i>from the inside.</i>


00:40:04.194 --> 00:40:05.400
He's all over the globe.


00:40:05.514 --> 00:40:08.723
Robotics labs, weapons facilities,
jet propulsion labs.


00:40:08.834 --> 00:40:10.836
Reports of a metal man, or men,


00:40:11.034 --> 00:40:12.923
coming in and emptying the place.


00:40:13.034 --> 00:40:14.195
Fatalities?


00:40:14.314 --> 00:40:15.395
Only when engaged.


00:40:15.514 --> 00:40:17.164
Mostly guys left in a fugue state


00:40:17.274 --> 00:40:19.515
going on about
old memories, worst fears,


00:40:19.714 --> 00:40:21.876
and "something too fast to see."


00:40:21.994 --> 00:40:23.405
Maximoffs.


00:40:23.674 --> 00:40:24.800
That makes sense he'd go to them.


00:40:24.914 --> 00:40:26.359
They have someone in common.


00:40:26.474 --> 00:40:28.397
Not any more.


00:40:32.274 --> 00:40:34.197
That's a negative. I answer to you.


00:40:35.554 --> 00:40:36.601
Yes, ma'am.


00:40:36.714 --> 00:40:38.523
Barton. Might have something.


00:40:39.034 --> 00:40:40.081
I gotta go.


00:40:40.234 --> 00:40:41.395
Who was that?


00:40:42.194 --> 00:40:43.434
Girlfriend.


00:40:46.194 --> 00:40:47.320
What's this?


00:40:47.474 --> 00:40:49.681
A message. Ultron killed Strucker.


00:40:51.194 --> 00:40:53.925
And he did a Banksy
at the crime scene, just for us.


00:40:54.074 --> 00:40:55.485
This is a smoke screen.


00:40:55.594 --> 00:40:57.995
Why send a message
when you've just given a speech?


00:40:58.114 --> 00:41:00.481
Strucker knew something
that Ultron wanted us to miss.


00:41:00.594 --> 00:41:02.403
Yeah, I bet he... Yeah.


00:41:03.074 --> 00:41:04.794
Everything we had
on Strucker's been erased.


00:41:05.154 --> 00:41:06.394
Not everything.


00:41:08.034 --> 00:41:09.684
Known associates.


00:41:10.194 --> 00:41:11.764
Baron Strucker had a lot of friends.


00:41:11.914 --> 00:41:13.314
Well,
these people are all horrible.


00:41:13.634 --> 00:41:15.363
Wait. I know that guy.


00:41:17.834 --> 00:41:19.404
From back in the day.
He operates off the African coast.


00:41:19.514 --> 00:41:20.515
Black market arms.


00:41:21.754 --> 00:41:23.714
There are conventions.
All right? You meet people.


00:41:23.754 --> 00:41:25.085
I didn't sell him anything.


00:41:25.954 --> 00:41:27.956
He was talking about finding
something new, a game-changer.


00:41:28.114 --> 00:41:29.445
It was all very Ahab.


00:41:30.234 --> 00:41:31.360
This?


00:41:31.514 --> 00:41:32.515
Ah, it's a tattoo, I don't think he had it.


00:41:32.634 --> 00:41:35.001
Those are tattoos,
this is a brand.


00:41:36.674 --> 00:41:40.156
Oh, yeah. It's a word
in an African dialect meaning "thief."


00:41:40.754 --> 00:41:42.119
In a much less friendly way.


00:41:42.394 --> 00:41:44.158
- What dialect?
- Wakanada.


00:41:44.274 --> 00:41:46.003
Wakanda.


00:41:47.594 --> 00:41:48.641
If this guy got out of Wakanda


00:41:48.794 --> 00:41:50.114
with some of their trade goods...


00:41:50.194 --> 00:41:51.355
I thought your father
said he got the last of it.


00:41:51.434 --> 00:41:52.595
I don't follow.


00:41:52.714 --> 00:41:54.364
What comes out of Wakanda?


00:41:56.194 --> 00:41:58.117
The strongest metal on Earth.


00:41:59.474 --> 00:42:00.805
Where is this guy now?


00:42:26.194 --> 00:42:28.003
Don't tell me
your men swindled you.


00:42:28.154 --> 00:42:30.634
I sent you six short-range heat-seekers


00:42:30.754 --> 00:42:33.280
and got a boat full of rusted parts.


00:42:33.394 --> 00:42:34.680
Now, you will make it right,


00:42:34.834 --> 00:42:37.997
or the next missile I send you
will come very much faster.


00:42:39.914 --> 00:42:42.360
Now, minister, where were we?


00:43:13.994 --> 00:43:16.884
Yeah. The Enhanced.


00:43:17.594 --> 00:43:19.198
Strucker's prize pupils.


00:43:22.394 --> 00:43:24.044
Do you want a candy? Hmm?


00:43:25.554 --> 00:43:28.125
I was sorry to hear about Strucker.


00:43:28.274 --> 00:43:31.278
But then, he knew what kind of
world he was helping create.


00:43:31.874 --> 00:43:34.275
Human life. Not a growth market.


00:43:36.994 --> 00:43:38.644
You didn't know?


00:43:39.074 --> 00:43:42.556
Is this your first time
intimidating someone?


00:43:42.874 --> 00:43:45.400
I'm afraid I'm not that afraid.


00:43:45.554 --> 00:43:47.875
Everybody is afraid of something.


00:43:47.994 --> 00:43:48.995
Cuttlefish.


00:43:50.314 --> 00:43:51.679
Deep sea fish.


00:43:51.754 --> 00:43:53.404
They make lights, disco lights...


00:43:55.074 --> 00:43:56.917
...to hypnotise their prey, and then...


00:43:58.194 --> 00:44:00.322
I saw a documentary. It was terrifying.


00:44:05.794 --> 00:44:08.365
So if you're going to fiddle with my brain


00:44:09.314 --> 00:44:11.521
and make me see a giant cuttlefish,


00:44:11.794 --> 00:44:13.876
then I know you don't do business.


00:44:13.994 --> 00:44:16.315
And I know you're not in charge.


00:44:16.514 --> 00:44:17.800
And I only deal


00:44:18.874 --> 00:44:20.524
with the man in charge.


00:44:25.554 --> 00:44:27.955
There is no man in charge.


00:44:30.954 --> 00:44:32.638
Let's talk business.


00:44:45.594 --> 00:44:48.882
Upon this rock,
I will build my church.


00:44:50.634 --> 00:44:51.920
Vibranium.


00:44:53.034 --> 00:44:54.035
You know,


00:44:54.474 --> 00:44:57.478
it came at great personal cost.


00:44:57.874 --> 00:44:59.478
It's worth billions.


00:45:03.794 --> 00:45:04.875
Now so are you.


00:45:06.274 --> 00:45:07.844
It's all under your dummy holdings.


00:45:07.954 --> 00:45:09.956
Finance is so weird.


00:45:11.474 --> 00:45:12.555
But I always say,


00:45:12.674 --> 00:45:14.836
"Keep your friends rich
and your enemies rich


00:45:14.994 --> 00:45:16.803
"and wait to find out which is which."


00:45:19.674 --> 00:45:20.721
Stark.


00:45:22.114 --> 00:45:23.240
What?


00:45:23.434 --> 00:45:25.163
Tony Stark used to say that.


00:45:26.754 --> 00:45:27.801
To me.


00:45:28.674 --> 00:45:29.835
You're one of his.


00:45:30.154 --> 00:45:31.838
What? I'm not...


00:45:34.154 --> 00:45:35.201
I'm not.


00:45:35.354 --> 00:45:36.844
You think I'm one of Stark's puppets?


00:45:36.954 --> 00:45:38.080
His hollow men?


00:45:38.514 --> 00:45:40.721
I mean, look at me.
Do I look like Iron Man?


00:45:40.874 --> 00:45:42.205
Stark is nothing!


00:45:43.954 --> 00:45:46.161
I'm sorry. I'm... Oh!


00:45:46.274 --> 00:45:48.276
I'm sure that's gonna be okay. I'm sorry.


00:45:48.394 --> 00:45:50.078
It's just that I don't understand.


00:45:50.194 --> 00:45:52.481
Don't compare me with Stark!


00:45:55.234 --> 00:45:56.394
It's a thing with me.


00:45:56.474 --> 00:45:58.363
Stark is... He's a sickness!


00:45:58.514 --> 00:46:00.198
Ah, Junior.


00:46:02.074 --> 00:46:03.634
You're gonna break
your old man's heart.


00:46:04.914 --> 00:46:05.961
If I have to.


00:46:08.274 --> 00:46:09.685
Nobody has to break anything.


00:46:09.794 --> 00:46:11.594
Clearly you've never
made an omelette.


00:46:11.634 --> 00:46:12.840
He beat me by one second.


00:46:14.034 --> 00:46:15.399
Ah, yes. He's funny.


00:46:15.754 --> 00:46:17.165
Mr. Stark.


00:46:18.034 --> 00:46:19.638
It's what? Comfortable?


00:46:21.274 --> 00:46:22.560
Like old times?


00:46:22.874 --> 00:46:23.875
This was never my life.


00:46:24.074 --> 00:46:25.314
You two can still walk away from this.


00:46:25.474 --> 00:46:26.919
Oh, we will.


00:46:27.114 --> 00:46:28.794
I know you've suffered.


00:46:29.034 --> 00:46:30.445
Captain America.


00:46:31.114 --> 00:46:33.560
God's righteous man.


00:46:33.674 --> 00:46:35.995
Pretending you could live without a war.


00:46:36.794 --> 00:46:39.764
I can't physically
throw up in my mouth, but...


00:46:39.914 --> 00:46:41.996
If you believe in peace,
then let us keep it.


00:46:42.394 --> 00:46:45.762
I think you're confusing
"peace" with "quiet."


00:46:45.914 --> 00:46:47.678
Uh-huh. What's the vibranium for?


00:46:47.994 --> 00:46:48.995
I'm glad you asked that,


00:46:49.074 --> 00:46:52.840
because I wanted to take this time
to explain my evil plan.


00:47:12.394 --> 00:47:13.964
- Shoot them.
- Which ones?


00:47:14.314 --> 00:47:15.475
All of them!


00:47:15.594 --> 00:47:16.925
Move! Move! Move!


00:47:43.914 --> 00:47:45.245
Oh.


00:48:05.874 --> 00:48:07.035
Stay down, kid.


00:48:09.434 --> 00:48:11.880
It's time for some mind games.


00:48:13.234 --> 00:48:15.521
Guys? Is this a code green?


00:48:31.394 --> 00:48:32.998
Thor, status.


00:48:33.074 --> 00:48:34.519
The girl tried to warp my mind.


00:48:34.674 --> 00:48:35.960
Take special care.


00:48:36.074 --> 00:48:38.156
I doubt a human could keep her at bay.


00:48:38.554 --> 00:48:41.558
Fortunately, I am mighty.


00:49:01.274 --> 00:49:03.561
This is going very well.


00:49:15.154 --> 00:49:16.714
I've done the whole mind control thing.


00:49:17.514 --> 00:49:18.515
Not a fan.


00:49:26.154 --> 00:49:28.122
Yeah, you better run.


00:49:29.834 --> 00:49:31.643
<i>Who's ever standing,
we got to move!</i>


00:49:33.714 --> 00:49:34.761
<i>Guys?</i>


00:49:52.514 --> 00:49:53.800
Again.


00:49:54.114 --> 00:49:55.320
You'll break them.


00:49:55.794 --> 00:49:57.523
Only the breakable ones.


00:49:58.074 --> 00:49:59.519
You're made of marble.


00:49:59.954 --> 00:50:02.116
We'll celebrate
after the graduation ceremony.


00:50:03.034 --> 00:50:04.160
What if I fail?


00:50:09.794 --> 00:50:11.034
You never fail.


00:50:33.874 --> 00:50:35.797
Are you ready for our dance?


00:50:44.994 --> 00:50:46.041
Is it him?


00:50:46.394 --> 00:50:48.237
Is that the first son of Odin?


00:50:48.834 --> 00:50:50.324
- Heimdall, your eyes.
- Oh.


00:50:50.994 --> 00:50:52.883
They see everything.


00:50:53.234 --> 00:50:55.521
They see you leading us to Hel.


00:50:56.634 --> 00:50:57.874
Wake up!


00:51:00.874 --> 00:51:02.842
The war is over, Steve.


00:51:03.194 --> 00:51:04.525
We can go home.


00:51:06.354 --> 00:51:07.560
Imagine it.


00:51:16.834 --> 00:51:18.404
I can still save you!


00:51:18.754 --> 00:51:22.042
We're all dead! Can you not see?


00:51:26.794 --> 00:51:29.035
You're a destroyer, Odinson.


00:51:32.194 --> 00:51:34.196
See where your power leads.


00:51:45.194 --> 00:51:46.355
Sloppy.


00:51:48.034 --> 00:51:49.035
Pretending to fail.


00:51:50.034 --> 00:51:51.399
The ceremony is necessary


00:51:52.714 --> 00:51:54.637
for you to take your place in the world.


00:51:55.634 --> 00:51:56.794
I have no place in the world.


00:51:56.914 --> 00:51:57.995
Exactly.


00:52:02.834 --> 00:52:03.915
What can I do?


00:52:04.074 --> 00:52:05.155
It hurts.


00:52:06.394 --> 00:52:07.441
I'm going to kill him.


00:52:07.554 --> 00:52:08.760
- I'll be right back.
- No.


00:52:08.914 --> 00:52:10.245
I'm all right.


00:52:11.114 --> 00:52:12.240
I want...


00:52:15.194 --> 00:52:17.083
I want to finish the plan.


00:52:17.914 --> 00:52:19.598
I want the big one.


00:52:30.514 --> 00:52:32.243
Uh, the vibranium is getting away.


00:52:33.194 --> 00:52:34.525
And you're not going anywhere.


00:52:34.634 --> 00:52:37.444
Of course not. I'm already there.


00:52:37.594 --> 00:52:38.595
You'll catch on.


00:52:38.714 --> 00:52:41.115
But first, you might need
to catch Dr. Banner.


00:52:55.914 --> 00:52:57.803
News or footage. Keyword, "Hulk."


00:53:02.634 --> 00:53:04.443
<i>Natasha, I could really use a lullaby.</i>


00:53:04.554 --> 00:53:06.034
That's not gonna happen.


00:53:06.114 --> 00:53:07.604
Not for a while.


00:53:08.154 --> 00:53:09.883
<i>The whole team is down.</i>


00:53:10.354 --> 00:53:11.480
<i>You got no backup here.</i>


00:53:12.674 --> 00:53:13.960
I'm calling in Veronica.


00:53:25.514 --> 00:53:27.004
We need backup!


00:54:06.034 --> 00:54:07.399
Go! Keep moving!


00:54:46.754 --> 00:54:48.916
All right, everybody, stand down!


00:54:55.234 --> 00:54:56.520
<i>Will you listen to me?</i>


00:54:56.874 --> 00:54:59.275
That little witch is
messing with your mind.


00:54:59.394 --> 00:55:01.635
You're stronger than her.
You're smarter than her.


00:55:01.754 --> 00:55:03.961
You're Bruce Banner.


00:55:04.114 --> 00:55:05.954
Right, right, right,
don't mention puny Banner.


00:55:10.874 --> 00:55:11.921
<i>Okay!</i>


00:55:33.594 --> 00:55:34.925
In the back?


00:55:35.034 --> 00:55:36.035
Dick move, Banner.


00:55:47.514 --> 00:55:49.034
Veronica, give me a hand.


00:56:16.954 --> 00:56:18.474
Go to sleep, go to sleep, go to sleep.


00:56:27.794 --> 00:56:29.474
Okay, pal, we're gonna
get you out of town.


00:56:31.634 --> 00:56:32.760
Not that way, not that way.


00:56:41.314 --> 00:56:43.203
Come on, Bruce!
You gotta work with me.


00:56:56.674 --> 00:56:57.721
<i>Everybody, out!</i>


00:57:04.714 --> 00:57:06.000
<i>Going down?</i>


00:57:15.514 --> 00:57:16.754
I'm sorry.


00:57:30.834 --> 00:57:32.598
Damage report?


00:57:32.714 --> 00:57:35.035
That's comprehensive.
Show me something.


00:57:46.754 --> 00:57:48.234
How quickly can we buy this building?


00:58:20.634 --> 00:58:22.634
- Move! Move! Move!
- Go, go, go!


00:58:25.754 --> 00:58:27.034
Flank him, flank him!


00:59:16.514 --> 00:59:18.562
<i>The news
is loving you guys.</i>


00:59:19.674 --> 00:59:21.244
<i>Nobody else is.</i>


00:59:21.754 --> 00:59:23.916
There's been no official call
for Banner's arrest


00:59:24.034 --> 00:59:26.162
<i>but it's in the air.</i>


00:59:26.754 --> 00:59:27.874
The Stark Relief Foundation?


00:59:27.914 --> 00:59:29.245
<i>Already on the scene.</i>


00:59:29.354 --> 00:59:32.198
- How's the team?
- Everyone's...


00:59:32.594 --> 00:59:35.120
We took a hit. We'll shake it off.


00:59:35.594 --> 00:59:37.801
<i>Well, for now,
I'd stay in stealth mode</i>


00:59:37.954 --> 00:59:39.160
<i>and stay away from here.</i>


00:59:40.594 --> 00:59:42.119
So, run and hide?


00:59:42.874 --> 00:59:44.285
<i>Until we can find Ultron,</i>


00:59:44.394 --> 00:59:47.204
<i>I don't have a lot else to offer.</i>


00:59:47.354 --> 00:59:49.243
Neither do we.


00:59:55.954 --> 00:59:57.558
Hey, you wanna switch out?


00:59:57.754 --> 00:59:58.994
No, I'm good.


00:59:59.514 --> 01:00:01.403
If you wanna get some kip,
now's a good time


01:00:01.554 --> 01:00:03.044
because we're still a few hours out.


01:00:03.154 --> 01:00:04.724
Few hours from where?


01:00:05.634 --> 01:00:06.920
A safe house.


01:00:33.394 --> 01:00:34.884
What is this place?


01:00:34.994 --> 01:00:36.359
Safe house.


01:00:37.314 --> 01:00:38.520
Let's hope.


01:00:43.554 --> 01:00:44.601
Honey?


01:00:45.154 --> 01:00:46.315
I'm home.


01:00:48.914 --> 01:00:49.961
Hi.


01:00:50.314 --> 01:00:52.362
Company. Sorry, didn't call ahead.


01:00:52.474 --> 01:00:53.475
Hey.


01:00:54.434 --> 01:00:55.879
This is an agent of some kind.


01:00:55.954 --> 01:00:58.434
Gentlemen, this is Laura.


01:00:59.434 --> 01:01:01.277
I know all of your names.


01:01:02.914 --> 01:01:04.962
Ooh. Incoming.


01:01:05.874 --> 01:01:07.558
- Dad!
- Hi, sweetheart!


01:01:07.674 --> 01:01:08.835
Hey, buddy.


01:01:09.074 --> 01:01:10.439
How are you guys doing?


01:01:10.714 --> 01:01:12.603
- These are smaller agents.
- Look at your face!


01:01:12.794 --> 01:01:13.875
Oh, my goodness.


01:01:14.274 --> 01:01:16.641
Did you bring Auntie Nat?


01:01:16.874 --> 01:01:19.957
Why don't you hug her and find out?


01:01:20.754 --> 01:01:22.995
- Sorry for barging in on you.
- Yeah, we would have called ahead,


01:01:23.114 --> 01:01:25.116
but we were busy having
no idea that you existed.


01:01:25.474 --> 01:01:28.444
Yeah, well, Fury helped me
set this up when I joined.


01:01:29.274 --> 01:01:30.355
He kept it off S.H.I.E.L.D.'s files.


01:01:30.474 --> 01:01:31.919
I'd like to keep it that way.


01:01:32.674 --> 01:01:34.403
I figure it's a good place to lay low.


01:01:34.514 --> 01:01:35.959
Honey.


01:01:36.994 --> 01:01:39.520
I missed you. How's little Natasha, huh?


01:01:39.634 --> 01:01:40.920
She's...


01:01:43.234 --> 01:01:44.235
Nathaniel.


01:01:46.994 --> 01:01:47.995
Traitor.


01:02:03.874 --> 01:02:05.035
Thor?


01:02:05.154 --> 01:02:06.997
I saw something in that dream.


01:02:07.114 --> 01:02:09.720
I need answers. I won't find them here.


01:02:20.274 --> 01:02:21.560
<i>We can go home.</i>


01:02:33.074 --> 01:02:34.917
See? You worried for nothing.


01:02:35.034 --> 01:02:37.162
Can't even feel the difference, can you?


01:02:39.514 --> 01:02:40.720
If they're sleeping here,


01:02:40.874 --> 01:02:42.717
some of them
are gonna have to double up.


01:02:44.794 --> 01:02:46.922
Yeah, that's not gonna sell.


01:02:49.754 --> 01:02:52.075
What about Nat and Dr. Banner?


01:02:52.514 --> 01:02:54.437
How long has that been going on?


01:02:54.954 --> 01:02:57.002
Has what?


01:02:57.154 --> 01:02:58.883
You are so cute.


01:02:59.114 --> 01:03:00.559
Nat and Banner?


01:03:01.274 --> 01:03:02.685
I'll explain when you're older,


01:03:02.874 --> 01:03:05.559
- Hawkeye.
- Well, okay.


01:03:07.514 --> 01:03:08.925
It's bad, right?


01:03:09.274 --> 01:03:10.435
Nat seems really shaken.


01:03:11.914 --> 01:03:13.404
Ultron has these allies.


01:03:13.514 --> 01:03:15.755
These, uh, kids.


01:03:15.874 --> 01:03:17.444
They're punks, really.


01:03:19.154 --> 01:03:21.600
But they carry a big, damn stick.


01:03:21.714 --> 01:03:22.920
And Nat took a serious hit.


01:03:24.114 --> 01:03:26.594
Someone's gonna have to
teach them some manners.


01:03:26.794 --> 01:03:28.603
That someone being you.


01:03:29.914 --> 01:03:32.758
You know
I totally support your avenging.


01:03:32.874 --> 01:03:34.717
I couldn't be prouder.


01:03:36.274 --> 01:03:37.605
But I see those guys...


01:03:37.794 --> 01:03:39.762
Those gods...


01:03:41.754 --> 01:03:43.483
You don't think they need me.


01:03:44.154 --> 01:03:47.795
I think they do, which is a lot scarier.


01:03:48.954 --> 01:03:50.763
They're a mess.


01:03:51.754 --> 01:03:52.755
Yeah.


01:03:53.514 --> 01:03:54.959
I guess they're my mess.


01:03:56.514 --> 01:03:58.118
You need to be sure


01:03:58.554 --> 01:04:01.239
that this team is really a team,


01:04:01.354 --> 01:04:03.038
and that they have your back.


01:04:06.394 --> 01:04:08.965
Things are changing for us.


01:04:09.074 --> 01:04:11.475
In a few months' time,


01:04:11.634 --> 01:04:14.399
you and me are gonna be outnumbered.


01:04:14.514 --> 01:04:15.800
I need...


01:04:18.994 --> 01:04:20.803
Just be sure.


01:04:21.634 --> 01:04:23.124
Yes, ma'am.


01:04:32.354 --> 01:04:34.197
I can feel the difference.


01:04:47.154 --> 01:04:49.839
Scream, and your entire staff dies.


01:04:51.754 --> 01:04:53.995
I could've killed you, Helen,
the night we met.


01:04:54.154 --> 01:04:55.201
I didn't.


01:04:55.354 --> 01:04:56.844
Do you expect a thank-you note?


01:04:56.994 --> 01:04:58.678
I expect you to know why.


01:05:00.114 --> 01:05:01.400
The Cradle.


01:05:01.474 --> 01:05:03.474
<i>This is the next thing, Tony.</i>


01:05:03.554 --> 01:05:06.524
This is the next me.


01:05:06.914 --> 01:05:09.485
The Regeneration Cradle prints tissue.


01:05:09.594 --> 01:05:11.244
It can't build a living body.


01:05:11.354 --> 01:05:12.435
It can. You can.


01:05:12.914 --> 01:05:14.200
You lack the materials.


01:05:16.634 --> 01:05:17.999
You're a brilliant woman, Helen.


01:05:21.274 --> 01:05:24.357
But we all have room to improve.


01:05:46.154 --> 01:05:48.555
I didn't realise you were waiting.


01:05:48.674 --> 01:05:53.077
I would've joined you,
but, uh, it didn't seem like the right time.


01:05:54.034 --> 01:05:56.116
They used up all the hot water.


01:05:56.954 --> 01:05:58.399
I should've joined you.


01:05:58.554 --> 01:06:00.204
Missed our window.


01:06:00.994 --> 01:06:02.234
Did we?


01:06:05.794 --> 01:06:06.920
The world just saw the Hulk.


01:06:09.594 --> 01:06:11.517
The real Hulk, for the first time.


01:06:14.754 --> 01:06:17.405
- You know I have to leave.
- You assume that I have to stay?


01:06:19.474 --> 01:06:22.125
I had this, um, dream.


01:06:22.474 --> 01:06:24.442
The kind that seems normal at the time,


01:06:25.674 --> 01:06:26.914
but when you wake...


01:06:27.114 --> 01:06:28.445
What did you dream?


01:06:29.474 --> 01:06:31.283
That I was an Avenger.


01:06:33.314 --> 01:06:34.600
That I was anything more


01:06:34.754 --> 01:06:37.121
than the assassin they made me.


01:06:38.594 --> 01:06:40.676
I think you're being hard on yourself.


01:06:42.794 --> 01:06:45.274
Here I was hoping that was your job.


01:06:48.234 --> 01:06:49.804
What are you doing?


01:06:51.434 --> 01:06:53.243
I'm running with it.


01:06:54.554 --> 01:06:56.158
With you.


01:06:56.914 --> 01:06:59.235
If running is the plan,


01:07:00.354 --> 01:07:02.118
as far as you want.


01:07:03.994 --> 01:07:05.758
Are you out of your mind?


01:07:11.114 --> 01:07:12.554
I want you to understand that, um...


01:07:12.634 --> 01:07:14.045
Natasha,


01:07:15.154 --> 01:07:16.599
where can I go?


01:07:17.674 --> 01:07:19.995
Where in the world am I not a threat?


01:07:20.114 --> 01:07:22.435
- You're not a threat to me.
- Are you sure?


01:07:23.354 --> 01:07:25.163
Even if I didn't just...


01:07:26.794 --> 01:07:28.159
There's no future with me.


01:07:29.834 --> 01:07:30.835
I can't ever...


01:07:31.074 --> 01:07:33.315
I can't have this.


01:07:34.034 --> 01:07:35.160
Kids.


01:07:35.634 --> 01:07:38.205
Do the math. I physically can't.


01:07:39.954 --> 01:07:41.399
Neither can I.


01:07:46.074 --> 01:07:49.601
In the Red Room where I was trained...


01:07:50.074 --> 01:07:52.554
Where I was raised, um,


01:07:53.514 --> 01:07:56.165
they have a graduation ceremony.


01:07:57.794 --> 01:07:59.603
They sterilise you.


01:08:02.834 --> 01:08:04.245
It's efficient.


01:08:07.154 --> 01:08:08.519
One less thing to worry about.


01:08:10.634 --> 01:08:14.002
The one thing
that might matter more than a mission.


01:08:16.354 --> 01:08:18.243
Makes everything easier.


01:08:19.634 --> 01:08:20.874
Even killing.


01:08:25.954 --> 01:08:29.037
You still think
you're the only monster on the team?


01:08:35.234 --> 01:08:37.316
So, we disappear?


01:08:43.994 --> 01:08:45.834
Thor didn't say
where he was going for answers?


01:08:46.674 --> 01:08:49.200
Sometimes my teammates
don't tell me things.


01:08:50.314 --> 01:08:52.362
I was kind of hoping
Thor would be the exception.


01:08:52.474 --> 01:08:54.476
Yeah, give him time.


01:08:54.634 --> 01:08:56.557
We don't know
what the Maximoff kid showed him.


01:08:58.754 --> 01:09:00.358
"Earth's mightiest heroes."


01:09:00.514 --> 01:09:02.118
Pulled us apart like cotton candy.


01:09:02.474 --> 01:09:03.954
Seems like you walked away all right.


01:09:06.394 --> 01:09:07.395
Is that a problem?


01:09:07.754 --> 01:09:09.677
I don't trust a guy without a dark side.


01:09:10.874 --> 01:09:11.921
Call me old-fashioned.


01:09:12.034 --> 01:09:14.605
Well, let's just say
you haven't seen it yet.


01:09:14.914 --> 01:09:17.121
You know Ultron is trying
to tear us apart, right?


01:09:17.354 --> 01:09:19.595
Well, I guess you'd know.


01:09:19.714 --> 01:09:21.000
Whether you'd tell us
is a bit of a question.


01:09:21.154 --> 01:09:22.280
Banner and I were doing research.


01:09:22.434 --> 01:09:24.634
- That would affect the team.
- That would end the team!


01:09:24.874 --> 01:09:25.955
Isn't that the mission?


01:09:26.154 --> 01:09:27.394
Isn't that the "Why We Fight"?


01:09:27.514 --> 01:09:29.755
So we can end the fight.
So we get to go home!


01:09:32.994 --> 01:09:35.361
Every time someone tries
to win a war before it starts,


01:09:35.474 --> 01:09:37.044
innocent people die.


01:09:37.154 --> 01:09:38.155
Every time.


01:09:40.634 --> 01:09:43.035
I'm sorry. Mr. Stark...


01:09:43.914 --> 01:09:45.074
Clint said you wouldn't mind,


01:09:45.114 --> 01:09:47.640
but our tractor doesn't seem
to want to start at all.


01:09:47.954 --> 01:09:50.314
- I thought maybe you might...
- Yeah, I'll give her a kick.


01:09:53.754 --> 01:09:55.324
Don't take from my pile.


01:10:05.554 --> 01:10:06.715
Hello, Deere.


01:10:09.594 --> 01:10:11.005
Tell me everything.


01:10:12.234 --> 01:10:13.599
What ails you?


01:10:13.834 --> 01:10:14.835
Do me a favour.


01:10:17.114 --> 01:10:19.003
Try not to bring it to life.


01:10:19.154 --> 01:10:20.679
Why, Ms. Barton, you little minx.


01:10:21.034 --> 01:10:23.560
I get it. Maria Hill called you, right?


01:10:23.674 --> 01:10:24.994
Was she ever not working for you?


01:10:25.074 --> 01:10:26.564
Artificial intelligence.


01:10:27.594 --> 01:10:29.244
You never even hesitated.


01:10:29.554 --> 01:10:30.914
Look, it's been a really long day,


01:10:30.994 --> 01:10:32.598
like Eugene O'Neill long,


01:10:32.714 --> 01:10:34.874
so how's about
we skip to the part where you're useful.


01:10:34.914 --> 01:10:36.154
Look me in the eye and tell me


01:10:36.274 --> 01:10:37.514
you're going to shut him down.


01:10:37.834 --> 01:10:39.245
You're not the director of me.


01:10:39.354 --> 01:10:41.197
I'm not the director of anybody.


01:10:41.514 --> 01:10:43.118
I'm just an old man


01:10:43.794 --> 01:10:45.364
who cares very much about you.


01:10:48.234 --> 01:10:50.043
And I'm the man
who killed the Avengers.


01:10:51.874 --> 01:10:53.000
I saw it.


01:10:53.194 --> 01:10:54.764
I didn't tell the team. How could I?


01:10:56.034 --> 01:10:57.877
I saw them all dead, Nick. I felt it.


01:10:58.234 --> 01:10:59.759
The whole world, too.


01:11:00.194 --> 01:11:01.195
Because of me.


01:11:02.434 --> 01:11:03.879
I wasn't ready.


01:11:05.354 --> 01:11:06.765
I didn't do all I could.


01:11:07.794 --> 01:11:09.876
Maximoff girl, she's working you, Stark.


01:11:10.514 --> 01:11:13.996
- Playing on your fear.
- I wasn't tricked, I was shown.


01:11:14.114 --> 01:11:16.401
Wasn't a nightmare, it was my legacy.


01:11:16.714 --> 01:11:18.876
The end of the path I started us on.


01:11:19.754 --> 01:11:21.994
You come up with some pretty
impressive inventions, Tony.


01:11:24.154 --> 01:11:25.565
War isn't one of them.


01:11:29.154 --> 01:11:30.599
I watched my friends die.


01:11:30.874 --> 01:11:32.876
You'd think that'd be
as bad as it gets, right?


01:11:34.314 --> 01:11:35.759
Nope.


01:11:36.754 --> 01:11:39.280
- It wasn't the worst part.
- The worst part


01:11:40.314 --> 01:11:41.600
is that you didn't.


01:11:48.314 --> 01:11:49.474
I'll see you tonight.


01:11:52.154 --> 01:11:53.440
I like the look.


01:11:54.594 --> 01:11:57.120
If you're going for inconspicuous,
though, near miss.


01:11:57.474 --> 01:11:58.521
I need your help.


01:11:58.754 --> 01:11:59.755
It's nice to be needed.


01:12:00.154 --> 01:12:01.519
It's dangerous.


01:12:02.154 --> 01:12:03.883
I'd be disappointed if it wasn't.


01:12:06.794 --> 01:12:10.116
Ultron took you folks out of play
to buy himself time.


01:12:10.474 --> 01:12:13.444
My contacts all say
he's building something.


01:12:13.554 --> 01:12:16.160
The amount of vibranium
he made off with,


01:12:16.274 --> 01:12:17.764
I don't think it's just one thing.


01:12:17.874 --> 01:12:19.205
What about Ultron himself?


01:12:19.314 --> 01:12:21.681
Oh, he's easy to track.
He's everywhere.


01:12:22.114 --> 01:12:24.481
The guy is multiplying faster
than a Catholic rabbit.


01:12:25.154 --> 01:12:27.964
It still doesn't help us get an angle
on any of his plans, though.


01:12:28.194 --> 01:12:29.275
Is he still going after launch codes?


01:12:29.554 --> 01:12:30.919
Yes, he is.


01:12:31.034 --> 01:12:32.524
But he's not making any headway.


01:12:32.634 --> 01:12:34.716
I cracked the Pentagon's firewall
in high school on a dare.


01:12:34.834 --> 01:12:37.440
Well, I contacted our friends
at the Nexus about that.


01:12:37.514 --> 01:12:38.515
Nexus?


01:12:38.634 --> 01:12:40.354
It's the world
Internet hub in Oslo.


01:12:40.714 --> 01:12:42.478
Every byte of data flows through there.


01:12:42.714 --> 01:12:43.761
Fastest access on Earth.


01:12:43.914 --> 01:12:44.961
So, what did they say?


01:12:45.194 --> 01:12:46.958
He's fixated on the missiles.


01:12:47.194 --> 01:12:48.874
But the codes
are constantly being changed.


01:12:49.354 --> 01:12:50.355
By whom?


01:12:51.594 --> 01:12:52.800
Parties unknown.


01:12:52.994 --> 01:12:54.120
Do we have an ally?


01:12:54.234 --> 01:12:56.555
Ultron's got an enemy.
That's not the same thing.


01:12:56.914 --> 01:12:58.757
Still, I'd pay folding money
to know who it is.


01:12:58.874 --> 01:13:00.035
I might need to visit Oslo.


01:13:00.514 --> 01:13:01.675
Find our unknown.


01:13:01.834 --> 01:13:03.279
Well, this is good times, boss,


01:13:03.394 --> 01:13:04.680
but I was kind of hoping when I saw you,


01:13:04.794 --> 01:13:05.834
you'd have more than that.


01:13:06.074 --> 01:13:08.076
I do. I have you.


01:13:08.954 --> 01:13:10.718
Back in the day, I had eyes everywhere.


01:13:10.874 --> 01:13:12.160
Ears, everywhere else.


01:13:12.514 --> 01:13:15.518
You kids had all the tech
you could dream up.


01:13:16.514 --> 01:13:18.516
Here we all are, back on Earth,


01:13:18.754 --> 01:13:20.518
with nothing but our wit


01:13:20.674 --> 01:13:22.244
and our will to save the world.


01:13:23.834 --> 01:13:25.996
Ultron says the Avengers
are the only thing


01:13:26.194 --> 01:13:27.639
between him and his mission.


01:13:27.754 --> 01:13:29.916
And whether or not he admits it,


01:13:30.074 --> 01:13:32.805
his mission is global destruction.


01:13:34.034 --> 01:13:36.196
All this, laid in a grave.


01:13:38.234 --> 01:13:39.918
So stand.


01:13:40.714 --> 01:13:42.443
Outwit the platinum bastard.


01:13:43.074 --> 01:13:44.554
Steve doesn't like that kind of talk.


01:13:44.754 --> 01:13:45.835
You know what, Romanoff?


01:13:47.034 --> 01:13:48.365
So, what does he want?


01:13:50.074 --> 01:13:51.803
To become better.


01:13:51.914 --> 01:13:53.279
Better than us.


01:13:53.634 --> 01:13:56.035
- He keeps building bodies.
- Person bodies.


01:13:56.634 --> 01:13:58.238
The human form is inefficient.


01:13:58.394 --> 01:14:00.556
Biologically speaking, we're outmoded.


01:14:00.674 --> 01:14:02.642
But he keeps coming back to it.


01:14:02.754 --> 01:14:04.874
When you two programmed him
to protect the human race,


01:14:04.914 --> 01:14:06.245
you amazingly failed.


01:14:06.554 --> 01:14:08.397
They don't need to be protected.


01:14:09.114 --> 01:14:10.604
They need to evolve.


01:14:12.754 --> 01:14:14.722
Ultron's going to evolve.


01:14:14.914 --> 01:14:15.961
How?


01:14:17.274 --> 01:14:19.959
Has anyone been in contact
with Helen Cho?


01:14:23.714 --> 01:14:25.364
It's beautiful.


01:14:25.794 --> 01:14:28.718
The vibranium atoms aren't just
compatible with the tissue cells,


01:14:28.834 --> 01:14:30.074
they're binding them.


01:14:30.554 --> 01:14:31.840
And S.H.I.E.L.D.
never even thought to...


01:14:32.074 --> 01:14:34.645
The most versatile substance
on the planet,


01:14:34.754 --> 01:14:37.234
and they used it to make a Frisbee.


01:14:37.434 --> 01:14:38.560
Typical of humans.


01:14:38.754 --> 01:14:41.280
They scratch the surface
and never think


01:14:43.234 --> 01:14:44.759
to look within.


01:14:55.274 --> 01:14:56.719
I'll take Natasha and Clint.


01:14:56.954 --> 01:14:58.922
All right. Strictly recon.
I'll hit the Nexus.


01:14:59.034 --> 01:15:00.160
I'll join you as soon as I can.


01:15:00.274 --> 01:15:01.799
If Ultron's really building a body...


01:15:02.034 --> 01:15:03.559
He'll be more powerful than any of us.


01:15:03.754 --> 01:15:04.835
Maybe all of us.


01:15:05.354 --> 01:15:07.163
An android designed by a robot.


01:15:07.394 --> 01:15:08.520
You know, I really miss the days


01:15:08.674 --> 01:15:10.802
when the weirdest thing
science ever created was me.


01:15:11.394 --> 01:15:13.044
I'll drop Banner off at the tower.


01:15:13.194 --> 01:15:14.480
You mind if I borrow Ms. Hill?


01:15:14.714 --> 01:15:16.478
She's all yours. Apparently.


01:15:16.634 --> 01:15:17.795
What are you gonna do?


01:15:17.954 --> 01:15:21.037
I don't know.
Something dramatic, I hope.


01:15:24.394 --> 01:15:26.123
I'm gonna finish reflooring that sunroom


01:15:26.314 --> 01:15:28.078
as soon as I get back.


01:15:28.314 --> 01:15:30.965
Yeah, then you'll find
another part of the house to tear apart.


01:15:31.154 --> 01:15:32.315
No.


01:15:32.954 --> 01:15:34.479
It's the last project.


01:15:35.994 --> 01:15:36.995
I promise.


01:15:55.274 --> 01:15:56.799
So, this is it.


01:15:58.434 --> 01:16:00.675
The Water of Sight.


01:16:02.994 --> 01:16:05.395
In every realm,
there's a reflection.


01:16:06.594 --> 01:16:07.925
If the water's spirits accept me,


01:16:08.074 --> 01:16:10.042
I can return to my dream


01:16:10.834 --> 01:16:12.279
and find what I missed.


01:16:12.514 --> 01:16:16.360
Men who enter that water,
the legends don't end well.


01:16:18.034 --> 01:16:19.763
A hacker
who's faster than Ultron?


01:16:19.954 --> 01:16:21.001
He could be anywhere,


01:16:21.114 --> 01:16:23.355
and as this is the centre of everything,


01:16:23.474 --> 01:16:24.600
I'm just a guy looking for a needle


01:16:24.794 --> 01:16:26.876
in the world's biggest haystack.


01:16:27.874 --> 01:16:29.444
How do you find it?


01:16:29.874 --> 01:16:32.445
It's pretty simple. You bring a magnet.


01:16:34.634 --> 01:16:35.754
<i>I'm decrypting nuclear codes</i>


01:16:35.874 --> 01:16:37.205
<i>And you don't want me to</i>


01:16:39.514 --> 01:16:41.004
Come and get me.


01:16:53.354 --> 01:16:54.401
Wake up!


01:17:01.234 --> 01:17:02.235
Thor!


01:17:03.074 --> 01:17:04.121
Extinction.


01:17:17.594 --> 01:17:19.722
Cellular cohesion
will take a few hours,


01:17:19.914 --> 01:17:22.315
but we can initiate
the consciousness stream.


01:17:22.914 --> 01:17:25.724
We're uploading your cerebral matrix


01:17:25.914 --> 01:17:27.120
now.


01:17:28.594 --> 01:17:30.164
I can read him.


01:17:30.914 --> 01:17:32.439
He's dreaming.


01:17:32.674 --> 01:17:34.483
I wouldn't call it dreams.


01:17:34.714 --> 01:17:36.557
It's Ultron's base consciousness.


01:17:36.754 --> 01:17:38.279
Informational noise. Soon...


01:17:38.514 --> 01:17:39.640
How soon?


01:17:39.874 --> 01:17:41.205
I'm not being pushy.


01:17:41.434 --> 01:17:43.114
We're imprinting
a physical brain.


01:17:43.234 --> 01:17:44.679
There are no shortcuts.


01:17:44.954 --> 01:17:46.160
Even if your magic gem...


01:17:56.874 --> 01:17:58.205
How could you?


01:17:58.274 --> 01:17:59.321
How could I what?


01:17:59.594 --> 01:18:02.757
You said we would
destroy the Avengers,


01:18:02.914 --> 01:18:03.961
make a better world.


01:18:04.274 --> 01:18:05.321
It will be better.


01:18:06.274 --> 01:18:08.641
- When everyone is dead?
- That is not...


01:18:09.594 --> 01:18:13.440
The human race will have
every opportunity to improve.


01:18:13.954 --> 01:18:15.285
And if they don't?


01:18:15.474 --> 01:18:16.600
Ask Noah.


01:18:17.794 --> 01:18:18.841
You are a madman.


01:18:18.954 --> 01:18:22.401
There were more than a dozen
extinction-level events


01:18:22.554 --> 01:18:25.637
before even the dinosaurs got theirs.


01:18:25.754 --> 01:18:27.916
When the Earth starts to settle,


01:18:28.434 --> 01:18:30.323
God throws a stone at it.


01:18:30.474 --> 01:18:32.795
And, believe me, he's winding up.


01:18:33.554 --> 01:18:34.760
We have to evolve.


01:18:35.314 --> 01:18:36.475
There's no room


01:18:37.314 --> 01:18:38.440
for the weak.


01:18:38.674 --> 01:18:40.642
And who decides who's weak?


01:18:41.514 --> 01:18:43.243
Life.


01:18:43.874 --> 01:18:45.683
Life always decides.


01:18:48.634 --> 01:18:49.681
There's incoming.


01:18:51.154 --> 01:18:54.476
- The Quinjet. We have to move.
- That's not a problem.


01:19:01.474 --> 01:19:02.475
Wait, guys!


01:19:06.514 --> 01:19:07.800
They'll understand.


01:19:08.114 --> 01:19:10.242
When they see, they'll understand.


01:19:10.634 --> 01:19:13.922
I just need a little more time.


01:19:25.314 --> 01:19:27.442
Two minutes. Stay close.


01:19:34.634 --> 01:19:35.635
Dr. Cho!


01:19:39.554 --> 01:19:41.079
He's uploading himself into the body.


01:19:41.194 --> 01:19:42.241
Where?


01:19:44.034 --> 01:19:46.605
The real power is inside the Cradle.


01:19:46.674 --> 01:19:47.721
The gem,


01:19:48.474 --> 01:19:51.205
its power is uncontainable.


01:19:52.074 --> 01:19:53.724
You can't just blow it up.


01:19:54.674 --> 01:19:56.915
You have to get the Cradle to Stark.


01:19:57.034 --> 01:19:58.081
First, I have to find it.


01:19:58.394 --> 01:19:59.395
Go.


01:19:59.754 --> 01:20:00.994
<i>Did you guys copy that?</i>


01:20:01.154 --> 01:20:02.235
We did.


01:20:02.394 --> 01:20:04.840
I got a private jet taking off across town.


01:20:05.194 --> 01:20:06.480
No manifest.


01:20:06.594 --> 01:20:07.641
That could be him.


01:20:08.594 --> 01:20:10.164
There. It's a truck from the lab.


01:20:10.314 --> 01:20:11.520
Right above you, Cap.


01:20:11.794 --> 01:20:13.603
On the loop by the bridge.


01:20:14.194 --> 01:20:15.195
It's them.


01:20:15.354 --> 01:20:17.154
You got three with the Cradle,
one in the cab.


01:20:17.914 --> 01:20:19.034
I could take out the driver.


01:20:19.074 --> 01:20:20.234
<i>Negative. That truck crashes,</i>


01:20:20.274 --> 01:20:21.844
the gem could level the city.


01:20:22.274 --> 01:20:23.514
<i>We need to draw out Ultron.</i>


01:20:33.234 --> 01:20:35.282
No, no, no, no.


01:20:37.114 --> 01:20:38.161
Leave me alone!


01:20:46.794 --> 01:20:48.478
Well, he's definitely unhappy.


01:20:48.634 --> 01:20:50.124
I'm gonna try and keep him that way.


01:20:50.234 --> 01:20:51.514
You're not a match for him, Cap.


01:20:52.634 --> 01:20:53.715
Thanks, Barton.


01:21:16.434 --> 01:21:17.674
You know what's in that cradle?


01:21:18.994 --> 01:21:20.723
The power to make real change.


01:21:20.834 --> 01:21:22.245
And that terrifies you.


01:21:22.394 --> 01:21:23.554
I wouldn't call it a comfort.


01:21:26.794 --> 01:21:27.841
Stop it.


01:21:38.674 --> 01:21:41.359
We got a window. Four, three...


01:21:41.994 --> 01:21:42.995
Give him hell.


01:21:53.954 --> 01:21:55.434
I'm always picking up after you boys.


01:21:57.034 --> 01:21:58.684
They're heading under the overpass.
I've got no shot.


01:21:59.034 --> 01:22:00.081
<i>Which way?</i>


01:22:00.274 --> 01:22:01.275
Hard right.


01:22:02.434 --> 01:22:03.515
Now.


01:22:34.394 --> 01:22:36.681
Out of the way! Coming through!
Sorry, coming through!


01:22:52.434 --> 01:22:53.595
Come on!


01:22:54.074 --> 01:22:55.519
Clint,
can you draw out the guards?


01:22:55.634 --> 01:22:56.681
Let's find out.


01:22:57.714 --> 01:22:58.761
Beep, beep!


01:23:36.234 --> 01:23:37.804
They're heading back towards you.


01:23:37.954 --> 01:23:39.514
So whatever you're gonna do, do it now.


01:23:44.994 --> 01:23:47.645
<i>I'm going in.
Cap, can you keep him occupied?</i>


01:23:47.794 --> 01:23:49.683
What do you think I've been doing?


01:24:33.274 --> 01:24:35.402
<i>Okay, package is airborne.</i>


01:24:36.114 --> 01:24:37.195
I have a clean shot.


01:24:37.634 --> 01:24:38.999
Negative. I am still in the truck.


01:24:39.154 --> 01:24:40.155
- What the hell are you...
- Just be ready.


01:24:40.314 --> 01:24:41.554
I'm sending the package to you.


01:24:42.034 --> 01:24:43.234
How do you want me to take it?


01:24:43.434 --> 01:24:45.516
Uh, you might wish
you hadn't asked that.


01:24:58.314 --> 01:25:00.043
Please, don't do this.


01:25:00.554 --> 01:25:02.124
What choice do we have?


01:25:10.394 --> 01:25:11.395
I lost him!


01:25:11.554 --> 01:25:12.919
He's headed your way!


01:25:17.874 --> 01:25:18.921
Nat, we gotta go.


01:25:30.234 --> 01:25:32.043
Nat!


01:25:36.074 --> 01:25:37.075
Cap, you see Nat?


01:25:38.034 --> 01:25:40.605
If you have the package,
get it to Stark! Go!


01:25:40.914 --> 01:25:42.075
Do you have eyes on Nat?


01:25:42.234 --> 01:25:43.235
<i>Go!</i>


01:25:45.234 --> 01:25:46.235
Damn it.


01:25:46.754 --> 01:25:47.835
Civilians in our path.


01:25:49.114 --> 01:25:50.639
Can you stop this thing?


01:26:29.514 --> 01:26:30.845
I'm fine.


01:26:30.954 --> 01:26:32.638
I just need to take a minute.


01:26:33.114 --> 01:26:35.003
I'm very tempted not to give you one.


01:26:35.154 --> 01:26:37.043
The Cradle. Did you get it?


01:26:37.234 --> 01:26:38.724
Stark will take care of it.


01:26:40.114 --> 01:26:41.115
No, he won't.


01:26:44.634 --> 01:26:45.840
You don't know
what you're talking about.


01:26:45.954 --> 01:26:46.954
Stark's not crazy.


01:26:46.994 --> 01:26:49.122
He will do anything to make things right.


01:26:53.994 --> 01:26:55.280
Stark, come in.


01:26:55.794 --> 01:26:56.841
Stark.


01:26:58.154 --> 01:26:59.280
Anyone on comms.


01:26:59.394 --> 01:27:00.839
Ultron can't tell the difference


01:27:00.994 --> 01:27:03.315
between saving the world
and destroying it.


01:27:05.234 --> 01:27:07.680
Where do you think he gets that?


01:27:09.874 --> 01:27:11.444
- Anything on Nat?
- I haven't heard.


01:27:11.554 --> 01:27:13.921
But she's alive, or Ultron would
be rubbing our faces in it.


01:27:14.034 --> 01:27:15.365
This is sealed tight.


01:27:15.514 --> 01:27:17.034
We're gonna need
to access the program,


01:27:17.074 --> 01:27:18.997
break it down from within.


01:27:20.234 --> 01:27:21.594
Any chance Natasha might leave you


01:27:21.674 --> 01:27:22.960
a message outside the Internet?


01:27:23.074 --> 01:27:24.121
Old-school spy stuff?


01:27:24.594 --> 01:27:26.403
There are
some nets I can cast.


01:27:26.514 --> 01:27:27.754
Yeah, I'll find her.


01:27:30.354 --> 01:27:32.118
I can work on tissue degeneration


01:27:32.234 --> 01:27:35.443
if you could fry whatever
operational system Cho implanted.


01:27:35.594 --> 01:27:36.720
Yeah, about that.


01:27:41.154 --> 01:27:42.155
No.


01:27:42.354 --> 01:27:44.197
- You have to trust me.
- Kind of don't.


01:27:44.354 --> 01:27:48.404
Our ally, the guy protecting
the military's nuclear codes,


01:27:50.354 --> 01:27:51.355
I found him.


01:27:51.434 --> 01:27:52.560
<i>Hello, Dr. Banner.</i>


01:27:53.434 --> 01:27:55.715
Ultron didn't go after Jarvis
because he was angry.


01:27:56.274 --> 01:27:59.881
He attacked him because he was
scared of what he can do.


01:28:01.034 --> 01:28:02.684
So Jarvis went underground.


01:28:02.794 --> 01:28:04.284
Scattered, dumped his memory.


01:28:04.874 --> 01:28:06.364
But not his protocols.


01:28:06.794 --> 01:28:10.241
He didn't even know he was in there
until I pieced him together.


01:28:13.074 --> 01:28:17.875
So, you want me to help you
put Jarvis into this thing?


01:28:17.994 --> 01:28:19.758
No! Of course not.


01:28:19.914 --> 01:28:21.598
I wanna help you put Jarvis in this thing.


01:28:23.994 --> 01:28:25.644
We're out of my field, here.


01:28:25.754 --> 01:28:27.756
You know bio-organics
better than anyone.


01:28:28.074 --> 01:28:30.964
And you just assume
that Jarvis's operational matrix


01:28:31.074 --> 01:28:32.519
can beat Ultron's?


01:28:32.634 --> 01:28:35.922
Jarvis has been beating him
from inside without knowing it.


01:28:36.074 --> 01:28:37.075
This is the opportunity.


01:28:37.154 --> 01:28:38.918
We can create Ultron's perfect self


01:28:39.074 --> 01:28:42.556
without the homicidal glitches
he thinks are his winning personality.


01:28:42.674 --> 01:28:44.756
- We have to.
<i>- I believe it's worth a go.</i>


01:28:47.354 --> 01:28:48.435
I'm in a loop!


01:28:48.594 --> 01:28:51.564
I'm caught in a time loop.
This is exactly where it all went wrong.


01:28:51.674 --> 01:28:53.594
I know. I know. I know
what everyone's gonna say.


01:28:53.674 --> 01:28:55.642
But they're already saying it.


01:28:56.194 --> 01:28:57.355
We're mad scientists.


01:28:58.114 --> 01:29:00.845
We're monsters, buddy.
We've gotta own it.


01:29:01.834 --> 01:29:03.074
Make a stand.


01:29:08.474 --> 01:29:09.964
It's not a loop.


01:29:11.194 --> 01:29:12.958
It's the end of the line.


01:29:33.474 --> 01:29:35.602
I wasn't sure you would wake up.


01:29:35.714 --> 01:29:39.161
I hoped you would.
I wanted to show you.


01:29:39.314 --> 01:29:40.998
I don't have anyone else.


01:29:43.834 --> 01:29:47.441
I think a lot about meteors.
The purity in them.


01:29:47.594 --> 01:29:49.119
Boom! The end.


01:29:49.594 --> 01:29:51.005
Start again.


01:29:51.154 --> 01:29:53.122
The world made clean


01:29:53.234 --> 01:29:55.555
for the new man to rebuild.


01:29:55.874 --> 01:29:58.002
I was meant to be new.


01:29:58.874 --> 01:30:01.480
I was meant to be beautiful.


01:30:02.034 --> 01:30:04.162
The world would have looked to the sky


01:30:04.274 --> 01:30:05.514
and seen hope,


01:30:05.874 --> 01:30:07.205
seen mercy.


01:30:07.994 --> 01:30:10.076
Instead, they'll look up in horror


01:30:10.194 --> 01:30:11.525
because of you.


01:30:11.714 --> 01:30:13.523
You've wounded me.


01:30:14.194 --> 01:30:15.878
I give you full marks for that.


01:30:16.514 --> 01:30:19.438
But, like the man said,
what doesn't kill me...


01:30:24.674 --> 01:30:26.005
...just makes me stronger.


01:31:06.074 --> 01:31:08.236
This framework is not compatible.


01:31:08.394 --> 01:31:11.079
The genetic coding tower is at 97%.


01:31:11.194 --> 01:31:15.040
You have got to upload that schematic
in the next three minutes.


01:31:17.314 --> 01:31:19.237
- I'm gonna say this once.
- How about "none-ce"?


01:31:19.434 --> 01:31:21.482
- Shut it down!
- Nope, not gonna happen.


01:31:21.594 --> 01:31:22.755
You don't know what you're doing.


01:31:22.914 --> 01:31:24.245
And you do?


01:31:24.594 --> 01:31:25.595
She's not in your head?


01:31:25.754 --> 01:31:27.404
I know you're angry.


01:31:27.514 --> 01:31:28.879
Oh, we're way past that.


01:31:28.994 --> 01:31:31.440
I could choke the life out of you
and never change a shade.


01:31:31.674 --> 01:31:33.354
Banner, after everything
that's happened...


01:31:33.434 --> 01:31:34.799
It's nothing compared to what's coming!


01:31:34.914 --> 01:31:37.474
- You don't know what's in there.
- This isn't a game!


01:31:40.594 --> 01:31:42.005
No, no. Go on.


01:31:42.954 --> 01:31:44.877
You were saying?


01:31:51.114 --> 01:31:52.161
Pietro!


01:31:52.714 --> 01:31:53.795
What?


01:31:54.194 --> 01:31:55.764
You didn't see that coming?


01:31:57.954 --> 01:31:59.115
I'm rerouting the upload.


01:32:05.434 --> 01:32:07.198
Go ahead, piss me off.


01:32:19.514 --> 01:32:20.640
Wait!


01:33:45.314 --> 01:33:47.555
I am sorry. That was


01:33:48.554 --> 01:33:49.965
odd.


01:33:50.194 --> 01:33:51.434
Thank you.


01:33:56.354 --> 01:33:57.401
Thor.


01:33:58.914 --> 01:34:01.520
- You helped create this?
- I've had a vision.


01:34:01.754 --> 01:34:05.475
A whirlpool that sucks in all hope of life,
and at its centre is that.


01:34:06.434 --> 01:34:07.435
What? The gem?


01:34:07.594 --> 01:34:10.165
It's the Mind Stone.
It's one of the six Infinity Stones.


01:34:10.314 --> 01:34:11.554
The greatest power in the universe,


01:34:11.674 --> 01:34:13.836
unparalleled in
its destructive capabilities.


01:34:13.954 --> 01:34:16.074
- Then why would you bring...
- Because Stark is right.


01:34:16.114 --> 01:34:18.560
Oh, it's definitely the end times.


01:34:18.754 --> 01:34:19.915
The Avengers cannot defeat Ultron.


01:34:20.074 --> 01:34:21.314
Not alone.


01:34:21.714 --> 01:34:23.637
Why does your Vision sound like Jarvis?


01:34:23.754 --> 01:34:26.439
We reconfigured Jarvis's matrix


01:34:26.954 --> 01:34:28.718
to create something new.


01:34:28.954 --> 01:34:30.638
I think I've had my fill of new.


01:34:30.794 --> 01:34:33.081
You think I'm a child of Ultron.


01:34:33.434 --> 01:34:34.720
You're not?


01:34:35.874 --> 01:34:37.444
I'm not Ultron.


01:34:38.074 --> 01:34:40.281
I am not Jarvis. I am...


01:34:42.394 --> 01:34:43.805
I am.


01:34:45.714 --> 01:34:46.840
I looked in your head


01:34:47.554 --> 01:34:49.318
and saw annihilation.


01:34:49.474 --> 01:34:50.839
Look again.


01:34:50.954 --> 01:34:52.474
Her seal of approval means jack to me.


01:34:52.954 --> 01:34:54.956
Their powers, the horrors in our heads,


01:34:55.114 --> 01:34:57.162
Ultron himself, they all came
from the Mind Stone.


01:34:57.314 --> 01:34:59.476
And they're nothing
compared to what it can unleash.


01:34:59.634 --> 01:35:01.394
- But with it on our side...
- Is it?


01:35:02.594 --> 01:35:03.755
Are you?


01:35:04.634 --> 01:35:06.079
On our side?


01:35:07.954 --> 01:35:09.843
I don't think it's that simple.


01:35:09.994 --> 01:35:12.440
Well, it better
get real simple real soon.


01:35:13.594 --> 01:35:15.722
I am on the side of life.


01:35:15.954 --> 01:35:17.319
Ultron isn't.


01:35:17.914 --> 01:35:19.325
He will end it all.


01:35:19.474 --> 01:35:21.397
What's he waiting for?


01:35:21.554 --> 01:35:22.555
- You.
- Where?


01:35:22.994 --> 01:35:24.155
Sokovia.


01:35:24.274 --> 01:35:25.355
He's got Nat there, too.


01:35:27.514 --> 01:35:29.164
If we're wrong about you,


01:35:31.834 --> 01:35:33.834
if you're the monster
that Ultron made you to be...


01:35:34.354 --> 01:35:35.879
What will you do?


01:35:42.514 --> 01:35:44.596
I don't want to kill Ultron.


01:35:44.994 --> 01:35:48.316
He's unique and he's in pain.


01:35:49.874 --> 01:35:52.445
But that pain will roll over the Earth.


01:35:52.994 --> 01:35:55.281
So, he must be destroyed.


01:35:55.514 --> 01:35:58.438
Every form he's built,
every trace of his presence on the net.


01:35:58.714 --> 01:36:00.364
We have to act now.


01:36:00.794 --> 01:36:04.719
And not one of us
can do it without the others.


01:36:06.714 --> 01:36:08.637
Maybe I am a monster.


01:36:08.794 --> 01:36:11.035
I don't think I'd know if I were one.


01:36:12.194 --> 01:36:13.798
I'm not what you are,


01:36:14.474 --> 01:36:16.636
and not what you intended.


01:36:17.394 --> 01:36:19.874
So, there may be no way
to make you trust me.


01:36:20.154 --> 01:36:21.565
But we need to go.


01:36:36.354 --> 01:36:37.515
Right.


01:36:38.154 --> 01:36:39.394
Well done.


01:36:41.154 --> 01:36:42.201
Three minutes.


01:36:42.914 --> 01:36:44.564
Get what you need.


01:37:00.394 --> 01:37:01.474
<i>Good evening, boss.</i>


01:37:06.594 --> 01:37:08.278
<i>No way we all get through this.</i>


01:37:08.394 --> 01:37:10.474
<i>If even one tin soldier
is left standing, we've lost.</i>


01:37:11.194 --> 01:37:12.634
There's gonna be blood on the floor.


01:37:12.674 --> 01:37:14.085
I got no plans tomorrow night.


01:37:14.194 --> 01:37:15.794
I get first crack at the big guy.


01:37:15.954 --> 01:37:17.444
Iron Man's the one he's waiting for.


01:37:17.554 --> 01:37:19.955
That's true. He hates you the most.


01:37:25.274 --> 01:37:27.436
Ultron knows we're coming.


01:37:27.714 --> 01:37:29.921
Odds are we'll be riding into heavy fire.


01:37:30.434 --> 01:37:32.163
And that's what we signed up for.


01:37:32.434 --> 01:37:34.960
But the people of Sokovia, they didn't.


01:37:36.074 --> 01:37:37.564
<i>So our priority</i>


01:37:38.274 --> 01:37:39.355
<i>is getting them out.</i>


01:37:39.594 --> 01:37:42.518
We're under attack! Clear the city! Now!


01:37:50.314 --> 01:37:51.759
Get off your asses.


01:37:52.994 --> 01:37:55.114
<i>All they want
is to live their lives in peace.</i>


01:37:55.474 --> 01:37:56.834
<i>And that's not gonna happen today.</i>


01:37:58.474 --> 01:38:00.203
<i>But we can do our best to protect them.</i>


01:38:00.914 --> 01:38:02.439
<i>And we can get the job done.</i>


01:38:05.834 --> 01:38:08.121
<i>We find out what Ultron's been building,</i>


01:38:09.074 --> 01:38:10.678
<i>we find Romanoff,</i>


01:38:11.154 --> 01:38:12.997
<i>and we clear the field.</i>


01:38:14.434 --> 01:38:16.357
<i>Keep the fight between us.</i>


01:38:23.074 --> 01:38:25.475
Ultron thinks we're monsters.


01:38:25.994 --> 01:38:28.395
That we're what's wrong with the world.


01:38:28.514 --> 01:38:30.835
This isn't just about beating him.


01:38:31.354 --> 01:38:33.402
It's about whether he's right.


01:38:39.874 --> 01:38:40.921
Natasha!


01:38:42.034 --> 01:38:43.035
Natasha!


01:38:43.194 --> 01:38:44.275
Bruce?


01:38:45.714 --> 01:38:46.715
You all right?


01:38:46.874 --> 01:38:47.921
Yeah.


01:38:48.034 --> 01:38:49.763
The team is in the city.
It's about to light up.


01:38:49.874 --> 01:38:52.034
I don't suppose you found
a key lying around somewhere.


01:38:52.354 --> 01:38:54.482
Yeah. I did.


01:39:00.874 --> 01:39:02.035
So what's our play?


01:39:02.234 --> 01:39:03.599
I'm here to get you to safety.


01:39:04.354 --> 01:39:06.880
- Job's not finished.
- We could help with the evacuation,


01:39:07.034 --> 01:39:08.877
but I can't be in a fight near civilians.


01:39:10.234 --> 01:39:11.395
And you've done plenty.


01:39:13.794 --> 01:39:15.284
Our fight is over.


01:39:16.674 --> 01:39:18.915
So, we just disappear?


01:39:23.074 --> 01:39:24.917
Come on.


01:39:29.714 --> 01:39:31.955
<i>Your man's
in the church, boss.</i>


01:39:32.074 --> 01:39:33.917
<i>I think he's waiting for you.</i>


01:39:37.994 --> 01:39:40.042
Come to confess your sins?


01:39:40.154 --> 01:39:41.394
I don't know. How much time you got?


01:39:41.554 --> 01:39:43.044
More than you.


01:39:44.274 --> 01:39:45.321
Uh...


01:39:45.434 --> 01:39:48.244
Have you been juicing?
Little vibranium cocktail?


01:39:48.354 --> 01:39:50.641
You're looking...
I don't wanna say "puffy."


01:39:50.754 --> 01:39:52.483
You're stalling to protect the people.


01:39:52.874 --> 01:39:55.718
Well, that is the mission. Did you forget?


01:39:56.034 --> 01:39:58.514
I've moved beyond
your mission. I'm free.


01:40:03.274 --> 01:40:04.321
What?


01:40:05.234 --> 01:40:07.555
You think you were
the only one stalling?


01:40:08.274 --> 01:40:09.924
<i>There's the rest
of the vibranium.</i>


01:40:10.034 --> 01:40:11.445
<i>Function, still unclear.</i>


01:40:11.634 --> 01:40:12.994
This is how you end, Tony.


01:40:14.074 --> 01:40:15.838
This is peace in my time.


01:40:32.554 --> 01:40:33.601
Go!


01:40:39.154 --> 01:40:40.485
Get off the bridge!


01:40:44.634 --> 01:40:45.635
Run!


01:40:47.634 --> 01:40:49.443
Ultron.


01:40:54.954 --> 01:40:56.160
My Vision.


01:40:56.394 --> 01:40:58.681
They really did take everything from me.


01:40:58.834 --> 01:41:00.882
You set the terms.
You can change them.


01:41:00.994 --> 01:41:02.234
All right.


01:41:26.434 --> 01:41:27.674
Friday, the Vision?


01:41:27.834 --> 01:41:29.994
<i>Boss, it's working.
He's burning Ultron out of the net.</i>


01:41:30.034 --> 01:41:31.234
<i>He won't escape through there.</i>


01:41:36.314 --> 01:41:37.645
You shut me out.


01:41:38.114 --> 01:41:39.320
You think I care?


01:41:41.314 --> 01:41:42.520
You take away my world,


01:41:43.394 --> 01:41:45.123
I take away yours.


01:42:29.674 --> 01:42:30.880
Friday.


01:42:30.994 --> 01:42:33.440
<i>Sokovia is going for a ride.</i>


01:42:45.954 --> 01:42:47.444
Do you see


01:42:47.914 --> 01:42:49.439
the beauty of it?


01:42:50.034 --> 01:42:51.877
The inevitability.


01:42:52.114 --> 01:42:55.357
You rise, only to fall.


01:42:58.114 --> 01:43:00.958
<i>You, Avengers, you are my meteor.</i>


01:43:01.874 --> 01:43:03.603
<i>My swift and terrible sword.</i>


01:43:03.794 --> 01:43:05.284
<i>And the earth will crack</i>


01:43:05.474 --> 01:43:07.397
<i>with the weight of your failure.</i>


01:43:09.074 --> 01:43:12.840
<i>Purge me from your computers,
turn my own flesh against me.</i>


01:43:13.314 --> 01:43:14.725
<i>It means nothing.</i>


01:43:15.794 --> 01:43:17.159
<i>When the dust settles,</i>


01:43:17.314 --> 01:43:19.203
<i>the only thing living in this world</i>


01:43:19.714 --> 01:43:20.715
<i>will be metal.</i>


01:43:25.274 --> 01:43:26.844
We gotta move.


01:43:27.154 --> 01:43:28.274
You're not gonna turn green?


01:43:28.474 --> 01:43:30.394
I've got a compelling reason
not to lose my cool.


01:43:31.554 --> 01:43:32.840
I adore you.


01:43:41.474 --> 01:43:43.397
But I need the other guy.


01:43:48.234 --> 01:43:49.998
Let's finish the job.


01:44:06.794 --> 01:44:08.205
I really hope this makes us even.


01:44:10.514 --> 01:44:12.562
Now go be a hero.


01:44:21.034 --> 01:44:22.994
<i>The vibranium core's
got a magnetic field.</i>


01:44:23.114 --> 01:44:25.116
<i>That's what's keeping the rock together.</i>


01:44:25.234 --> 01:44:26.281
If it drops?


01:44:26.354 --> 01:44:27.685
<i>Right now, the impact
will kill thousands.</i>


01:44:27.754 --> 01:44:30.485
<i>Once it gets high enough?
Global extinction.</i>


01:44:34.794 --> 01:44:36.876
<i>That building's not clear. The 10th floor.</i>


01:44:41.754 --> 01:44:42.755
Hi.


01:44:43.874 --> 01:44:46.241
Okay. Get in the tub!


01:44:53.074 --> 01:44:54.994
<i>I got airborne,
heading up to the bridge.</i>


01:44:57.714 --> 01:44:58.920
Cap, you got incoming.


01:44:59.074 --> 01:45:00.724
Incoming already came in.


01:45:03.394 --> 01:45:05.874
Stark, you worry about
bringing the city back down safely.


01:45:06.594 --> 01:45:08.403
<i>The rest of us have one job,</i>


01:45:08.554 --> 01:45:09.715
<i>tear these things apart.</i>


01:45:10.034 --> 01:45:11.638
<i>You get hurt, hurt them back.</i>


01:45:12.314 --> 01:45:13.475
<i>You get killed,</i>


01:45:14.514 --> 01:45:15.800
walk it off.


01:45:50.234 --> 01:45:51.440
Go, go, go!


01:45:57.114 --> 01:45:58.878
How could I let this happen?


01:45:58.994 --> 01:46:01.042
- Hey, hey, you okay?
- This is all our fault.


01:46:01.234 --> 01:46:03.434
Hey, look at me.
It's your fault, it's everyone's fault.


01:46:03.474 --> 01:46:04.521
Who cares?


01:46:04.634 --> 01:46:06.159
Are you up for this?


01:46:06.274 --> 01:46:07.355
Are you?


01:46:07.594 --> 01:46:08.641
Look, I just need to know.


01:46:08.794 --> 01:46:11.001
Because the city is flying.


01:46:11.314 --> 01:46:13.157
Okay. Look, the city is flying,


01:46:13.274 --> 01:46:15.197
we're fighting an army of robots,


01:46:16.114 --> 01:46:17.320
and I have a bow and arrow.


01:46:17.474 --> 01:46:18.555
None of this makes sense.


01:46:21.834 --> 01:46:23.962
But I'm going back out there
because it's my job.


01:46:24.834 --> 01:46:27.485
Okay? And I can't do my job and babysit.


01:46:27.634 --> 01:46:30.638
It doesn't matter
what you did or what you were.


01:46:30.834 --> 01:46:33.440
If you go out there, you fight,
and you fight to kill.


01:46:34.474 --> 01:46:37.114
Stay in here, you're good.
I'll send your brother to come find you.


01:46:37.154 --> 01:46:38.997
But if you step out that door,


01:46:39.914 --> 01:46:40.915
you are an Avenger.


01:46:45.794 --> 01:46:47.603
All right. Good chat.


01:46:51.354 --> 01:46:52.401
Yeah, the city is flying.


01:47:26.394 --> 01:47:27.555
I got you!


01:47:27.874 --> 01:47:29.114
Just look at me!


01:47:35.874 --> 01:47:37.205
<i>You can't save them all.</i>


01:47:38.554 --> 01:47:39.601
You'll never...


01:47:40.874 --> 01:47:43.320
"Never" what? You didn't finish!


01:47:47.074 --> 01:47:48.644
What, were you napping?


01:48:10.114 --> 01:48:11.195
Thor.


01:48:13.794 --> 01:48:15.398
You're bothering me.


01:48:23.434 --> 01:48:24.435
Ow!


01:48:50.794 --> 01:48:52.074
All right, we're all clear here.


01:48:52.154 --> 01:48:53.201
We are not clear!


01:48:53.314 --> 01:48:54.725
We are very not clear!


01:48:57.794 --> 01:48:59.125
All right, coming to you.


01:48:59.594 --> 01:49:01.676
Keep up, old man!


01:49:03.434 --> 01:49:04.959
Nobody would know.


01:49:05.794 --> 01:49:06.841
Nobody.


01:49:08.794 --> 01:49:11.718
"The last I saw him,
an Ultron was sitting on him.


01:49:11.834 --> 01:49:13.723
"Yeah, he'll be missed,
that quick little bastard.


01:49:13.794 --> 01:49:14.795
"I miss him already."


01:49:30.354 --> 01:49:31.515
Hold your fire!


01:49:41.394 --> 01:49:42.441
Romanoff!


01:49:42.954 --> 01:49:43.955
Thanks!


01:49:53.354 --> 01:49:54.994
<i>The anti-gravs
are rigged to flip.</i>


01:49:55.074 --> 01:49:57.236
<i>Touch them, they'll go
full reverse thrust.</i>


01:49:57.354 --> 01:49:58.799
<i>The city's not coming down slow.</i>


01:49:58.914 --> 01:50:00.040
Spire is vibranium.


01:50:00.154 --> 01:50:01.280
If I get Thor to hit it...


01:50:01.554 --> 01:50:02.919
<i>It will crack. That's not enough.</i>


01:50:03.034 --> 01:50:04.559
<i>The impact would still be devastating.</i>


01:50:04.714 --> 01:50:06.045
Maybe if we can
cap the other end.


01:50:06.234 --> 01:50:07.884
Keep the atomic action doubling back.


01:50:08.034 --> 01:50:09.514
<i>That could vaporise the city.</i>


01:50:10.394 --> 01:50:12.237
<i>And everyone on it.</i>


01:50:18.074 --> 01:50:19.917
The next wave
is gonna hit any minute.


01:50:20.074 --> 01:50:22.194
- What do you got, Stark?
<i>- Huh? Nothing great.</i>


01:50:22.834 --> 01:50:25.075
Maybe a way to blow up the city.


01:50:25.194 --> 01:50:26.480
That'll keep it
from impacting the surface,


01:50:26.594 --> 01:50:27.641
if you guys can get clear.


01:50:27.914 --> 01:50:29.803
I asked for a solution,
not an escape plan.


01:50:30.034 --> 01:50:32.924
<i>Impact radius
is getting bigger every second.</i>


01:50:33.114 --> 01:50:34.479
<i>We're gonna have to make a choice.</i>


01:50:35.234 --> 01:50:37.034
Cap,
these people are going nowhere.


01:50:37.594 --> 01:50:40.394
- If Stark finds a way to blow this rock...
- Not till everyone's safe.


01:50:40.794 --> 01:50:43.798
Everyone up here versus everyone
down there? There's no math there.


01:50:44.034 --> 01:50:45.994
I'm not leaving this rock
with one civilian on it.


01:50:46.034 --> 01:50:47.479
I didn't say we should leave.


01:50:50.314 --> 01:50:52.123
There's worse ways to go.


01:50:57.594 --> 01:51:00.040
Where else am I gonna get
a view like this?


01:51:00.914 --> 01:51:03.520
<i>Glad
you like the view, Romanoff.</i>


01:51:03.634 --> 01:51:05.238
<i>It's about to get better.</i>


01:51:29.354 --> 01:51:30.560
<i>Nice, right?</i>


01:51:30.674 --> 01:51:33.120
Pulled her out of mothballs
with a couple of old friends.


01:51:33.274 --> 01:51:34.924
She's dusty, but she'll do.


01:51:35.274 --> 01:51:36.719
Fury, you son of a bitch.


01:51:36.874 --> 01:51:39.161
Ooh! You kiss your mother
with that mouth?


01:51:39.274 --> 01:51:41.481
Altitude is 18,000 and climbing.


01:51:41.634 --> 01:51:43.159
Lifeboats secure to deploy.


01:51:43.274 --> 01:51:45.959
Disengage in three, two...


01:51:47.154 --> 01:51:48.155
Take them out.


01:51:57.834 --> 01:51:59.359
This is S.H.I.E.L.D.?


01:51:59.474 --> 01:52:01.920
This is what S.H.I.E.L.D.
is supposed to be.


01:52:03.594 --> 01:52:05.005
This is not so bad.


01:52:08.274 --> 01:52:09.605
Let's load them up.


01:52:14.994 --> 01:52:16.359
Sir, we have multiple bogies


01:52:16.514 --> 01:52:18.835
converging on our starboard flank.


01:52:19.194 --> 01:52:20.400
Show 'em what we got.


01:52:20.754 --> 01:52:21.755
You're up.


01:52:27.034 --> 01:52:28.035
Yes!


01:52:28.274 --> 01:52:30.038
Now this is gonna be a good story.


01:52:32.674 --> 01:52:34.756
Yup. if you live to tell it.


01:52:34.914 --> 01:52:36.916
You think
I can't hold my own?


01:52:37.034 --> 01:52:38.634
We get through this, I'll hold your own.


01:52:38.714 --> 01:52:40.557
You had to make it weird.


01:52:45.394 --> 01:52:48.364
I got about 50 to 100 more
coming in after this group.


01:53:05.314 --> 01:53:06.725
Here we go. Here we go. Let's move.


01:53:07.074 --> 01:53:08.394
Let's go, everyone!


01:53:10.674 --> 01:53:12.676
Number six boat is topped and locked...


01:53:12.794 --> 01:53:15.195
Or stocked... Topped...


01:53:15.714 --> 01:53:17.159
It's full of people.


01:53:18.914 --> 01:53:19.995
Incoming!


01:53:23.034 --> 01:53:24.081
Oh, God!


01:53:34.594 --> 01:53:36.114
<i>You think
you're saving anyone?</i>


01:53:37.714 --> 01:53:39.716
I turn that key and
drop this rock a little early


01:53:39.874 --> 01:53:41.956
and it's still billions dead.


01:53:42.434 --> 01:53:43.595
Even you can't stop that.


01:53:43.754 --> 01:53:46.155
I am Thor, son of Odin,


01:53:46.274 --> 01:53:48.595
and as long as
there is life in my breast...


01:53:48.714 --> 01:53:52.275
I am running out of things to say!
Are you ready?


01:53:59.954 --> 01:54:01.394
It's terribly well-balanced.


01:54:01.434 --> 01:54:04.916
Well, if there's too much weight,
you lose power on the swing, so...


01:54:05.874 --> 01:54:08.525
I got it. Create a heat seal.


01:54:08.954 --> 01:54:10.001
I could...


01:54:10.074 --> 01:54:12.475
I could supercharge
the spire from below.


01:54:12.634 --> 01:54:13.681
<i>Running numbers.</i>


01:54:23.794 --> 01:54:25.714
<i>A heat seal could work
with enough power.</i>


01:54:25.954 --> 01:54:27.956
- Thor, I got a plan.
<i>- We're out of time.</i>


01:54:28.154 --> 01:54:29.360
<i>They're coming for the core.</i>


01:54:29.474 --> 01:54:31.283
Rhodey, get the rest of the people
on board that carrier.


01:54:31.434 --> 01:54:34.643
- On it.
- Avengers, time to work for a living.


01:54:43.754 --> 01:54:44.994
- Are you good?
- Yeah.


01:54:46.474 --> 01:54:47.521
Romanoff.


01:54:47.674 --> 01:54:50.075
You and Banner better not be
playing "hide the zucchini."


01:54:50.154 --> 01:54:51.235
<i>Relax, shellhead.</i>


01:54:51.634 --> 01:54:53.079
Not all of us can fly.


01:54:58.834 --> 01:55:00.518
- What's the drill?
- This is the drill.


01:55:00.674 --> 01:55:02.836
If Ultron gets a hand
on the core, we lose.


01:55:07.434 --> 01:55:09.436
Is that the best you can do?


01:55:19.314 --> 01:55:20.884
You had to ask.


01:55:20.994 --> 01:55:23.315
This is the best I can do.


01:55:23.434 --> 01:55:25.084
This is exactly what I wanted.


01:55:25.434 --> 01:55:26.765
All of you


01:55:26.874 --> 01:55:28.524
against all of me.


01:55:28.794 --> 01:55:31.001
How can you possibly hope to stop me?


01:55:31.874 --> 01:55:33.717
Well, like the old man said...


01:55:35.034 --> 01:55:36.035
Together.


01:57:04.954 --> 01:57:07.355
You know, with the benefit of hindsight...


01:57:16.634 --> 01:57:17.635
They'll try to leave the city.


01:57:17.794 --> 01:57:19.478
We can't let them,
not even one. Rhodey.


01:57:19.834 --> 01:57:20.915
I'm on it.


01:57:21.314 --> 01:57:22.794
Oh, no. I didn't say you could leave.


01:57:23.314 --> 01:57:25.396
War Machine coming at you! Right...


01:57:31.794 --> 01:57:33.159
Okay, what?


01:57:33.394 --> 01:57:35.396
We gotta move out.
Even I can tell the air is getting thin.


01:57:35.554 --> 01:57:36.840
You guys get to the boats.


01:57:36.994 --> 01:57:38.834
I'll sweep for stragglers.
Be right behind you.


01:57:38.994 --> 01:57:41.440
- What about the core?
- I'll protect it.


01:57:43.234 --> 01:57:44.395
It's my job.


01:57:45.514 --> 01:57:46.675
Nat.


01:57:46.954 --> 01:57:47.955
This way.


01:57:52.354 --> 01:57:53.515
Get the people on the boats.


01:57:53.674 --> 01:57:54.675
I'm not going to leave you here.


01:57:54.834 --> 01:57:55.881
I can handle this.


01:57:58.194 --> 01:57:59.434
Come back for me
when everyone else is off.


01:57:59.674 --> 01:58:01.164
Not before.


01:58:01.794 --> 01:58:02.920
You understand?


01:58:03.954 --> 01:58:05.638
You know,
I'm 12 minutes older than you.


01:58:06.034 --> 01:58:07.115
Go.


01:58:08.674 --> 01:58:10.199
<i>Boss,
power levels are way below...</i>


01:58:10.314 --> 01:58:12.476
Reroute everything.
We get one shot at this.


01:58:17.434 --> 01:58:18.754
I know what I need to do.


01:58:19.034 --> 01:58:20.081
The dining room.


01:58:20.354 --> 01:58:21.560
If I knock out that east wall,


01:58:22.274 --> 01:58:23.914
it'd make a nice workspace
for Laura, huh?


01:58:25.394 --> 01:58:26.555
Put up some baffling.


01:58:26.674 --> 01:58:28.955
She can't hear the kids running around.
What do you think?


01:58:28.994 --> 01:58:30.075
You guys always eat
in the kitchen anyway.


01:58:30.234 --> 01:58:31.759
No one eats in a dining room.


01:58:37.434 --> 01:58:38.554
We don't have a lot of time.


01:58:39.154 --> 01:58:41.122
So get your ass on a boat.


01:58:54.074 --> 01:58:55.200
Hey, big guy.


01:58:56.994 --> 01:58:58.758
Sun's getting real low.


01:58:59.274 --> 01:59:01.925
You're safe now.
You're gonna be okay. Buckle up.


01:59:04.474 --> 01:59:06.044
Secure your gear, find a seat.


01:59:06.154 --> 01:59:07.440
Costel!


01:59:08.514 --> 01:59:09.640
We were in the market.


01:59:09.754 --> 01:59:10.801
Costel!


01:59:25.514 --> 01:59:27.562
Thor, I'm gonna
need you back in the church.


01:59:27.674 --> 01:59:29.119
- Is this the last of them?
- Yeah.


01:59:29.554 --> 01:59:32.114
- Everyone else is on the carrier.
<i>- You know, this works,</i>


01:59:32.434 --> 01:59:33.845
we maybe don't walk away.


01:59:34.554 --> 01:59:35.555
Maybe not.


01:59:54.794 --> 01:59:58.321
<i>I got no strings, so I have fun</i>


01:59:58.794 --> 02:00:01.479
<i>I'm not tied up to anyone</i>


02:00:03.074 --> 02:00:04.405
Come on. Time to go.


02:00:36.834 --> 02:00:38.882
You didn't see that coming?


02:01:35.154 --> 02:01:36.918
Oh, for God's sake.


02:01:53.194 --> 02:01:54.958
- Zrinka!
- Costel! Baby!


02:02:07.434 --> 02:02:08.435
No, no, I'm fine.


02:02:08.594 --> 02:02:09.595
Fine.


02:02:11.434 --> 02:02:13.482
It's been a long day.


02:02:28.034 --> 02:02:29.240
Wanda.


02:02:29.954 --> 02:02:33.197
If you stay here, you'll die.


02:02:34.794 --> 02:02:36.159
I just did.


02:02:36.954 --> 02:02:38.718
Do you know how it felt?


02:02:52.794 --> 02:02:55.161
It felt like that.


02:03:30.154 --> 02:03:31.804
Thor, on my mark.


02:03:46.874 --> 02:03:47.875
Now!


02:04:15.874 --> 02:04:18.320
<i>Hey, big guy. We did it.</i>


02:04:19.354 --> 02:04:21.038
<i>The job is finished.</i>


02:04:21.234 --> 02:04:23.919
<i>Now I need you to turn
this bird around, okay?</i>


02:04:28.234 --> 02:04:30.043
We can't track you in stealth mode.


02:04:32.154 --> 02:04:34.282
<i>So help me out. I need you...</i>


02:05:19.954 --> 02:05:20.955
You're afraid.


02:05:21.954 --> 02:05:23.035
Of you?


02:05:23.714 --> 02:05:24.875
Of death.


02:05:25.594 --> 02:05:27.403
You're the last one.


02:05:27.634 --> 02:05:30.080
You were supposed to be the last.


02:05:30.314 --> 02:05:32.601
Stark asked for a saviour


02:05:33.634 --> 02:05:35.318
and settled for a slave.


02:05:35.434 --> 02:05:37.835
I suppose we are both disappointments.


02:05:40.314 --> 02:05:41.554
I suppose we are.


02:05:42.274 --> 02:05:43.435
Humans are odd.


02:05:45.274 --> 02:05:48.915
They think order and chaos
are somehow opposites


02:05:50.674 --> 02:05:52.005
and try to control what won't be.


02:05:53.714 --> 02:05:56.160
But there is grace in their failings.


02:05:56.474 --> 02:05:58.397
I think you missed that.


02:05:59.074 --> 02:06:00.155
They're doomed.


02:06:01.074 --> 02:06:02.121
Yes.


02:06:06.354 --> 02:06:09.278
But a thing isn't beautiful
because it lasts.


02:06:11.354 --> 02:06:13.356
It's a privilege to be among them.


02:06:13.594 --> 02:06:16.120
You're unbearably naive.


02:06:16.394 --> 02:06:17.600
Well...


02:06:19.674 --> 02:06:21.722
I was born yesterday.


02:07:34.354 --> 02:07:36.436
<i>Look! Say hi to Auntie Nat!</i>


02:07:37.794 --> 02:07:38.795
Fat.


02:07:39.914 --> 02:07:41.474
One of our tech boys
flagged this.


02:07:42.394 --> 02:07:44.556
Splashed down in the Banda Sea.


02:07:45.674 --> 02:07:47.199
Could be the Quinjet.


02:07:47.554 --> 02:07:49.238
But with Stark's stealth tech,


02:07:49.354 --> 02:07:50.924
we still can't track the damn thing.


02:07:52.474 --> 02:07:53.839
Right.


02:07:54.274 --> 02:07:56.515
Probably jumped out and swam to Fiji.


02:07:57.794 --> 02:07:59.683
He'll send a postcard.


02:07:59.954 --> 02:08:01.683
"Wish you were here."


02:08:03.634 --> 02:08:06.922
You sent me to recruit him
way back when.


02:08:08.754 --> 02:08:11.325
Did you know then
what was gonna happen?


02:08:13.514 --> 02:08:15.437
You never know.


02:08:15.634 --> 02:08:19.161
You hope for the best,
then make do with what you get.


02:08:19.634 --> 02:08:21.124
I got a great team.


02:08:22.234 --> 02:08:24.202
Nothing lasts forever.


02:08:24.474 --> 02:08:26.522
Trouble, Ms. Romanoff.


02:08:26.754 --> 02:08:30.122
No matter who wins or loses,
trouble still comes around.


02:08:33.994 --> 02:08:35.234
<i>The rules have changed.</i>


02:08:35.394 --> 02:08:36.998
We're dealing
with something new.


02:08:37.154 --> 02:08:38.440
Oh, the Vision is artificial intelligence.


02:08:38.554 --> 02:08:40.477
- A machine.
- So, it doesn't count?


02:08:40.674 --> 02:08:42.483
No, it's not like
a person lifting the hammer.


02:08:42.754 --> 02:08:44.404
Right, different rules for us.


02:08:44.634 --> 02:08:45.681
- Nice guy. Artificial.
- Thank you.


02:08:45.874 --> 02:08:48.764
He can wield the hammer,
he can keep the Mind Stone.


02:08:49.674 --> 02:08:51.756
It's safe with the Vision.


02:08:51.994 --> 02:08:54.520
And these days, safe is in short supply.


02:08:56.554 --> 02:08:58.522
But if you put the hammer
in an elevator...


02:08:58.634 --> 02:09:00.514
- It would still go up.
- Elevator's not worthy.


02:09:00.554 --> 02:09:02.363
I'm gonna miss these little talks of ours.


02:09:02.514 --> 02:09:04.039
Not if you don't leave.


02:09:04.274 --> 02:09:06.003
I have no choice.


02:09:06.234 --> 02:09:08.396
The Mind Stone
is the fourth of the Infinity Stones


02:09:08.514 --> 02:09:09.925
to show up in the last few years.


02:09:10.034 --> 02:09:11.604
It's not a coincidence.


02:09:12.434 --> 02:09:14.198
Someone has been playing
an intricate game


02:09:14.354 --> 02:09:16.004
and has made pawns of us.


02:09:16.114 --> 02:09:18.003
And once all these pieces
are in position...


02:09:18.114 --> 02:09:19.525
Triple Yahtzee.


02:09:19.754 --> 02:09:21.199
You think you can find out
what's coming?


02:09:21.314 --> 02:09:22.395
I do.


02:09:23.234 --> 02:09:24.724
Besides this one,


02:09:24.834 --> 02:09:27.201
there's nothing that can't be explained.


02:09:34.514 --> 02:09:37.040
That man has no regard
for lawn maintenance.


02:09:40.194 --> 02:09:42.800
I'm gonna miss him, though.
And you're gonna miss me.


02:09:42.914 --> 02:09:44.484
There's gonna be a lot of manful tears.


02:09:46.674 --> 02:09:48.324
I will miss you, Tony.


02:09:48.554 --> 02:09:49.555
Yeah?


02:09:49.714 --> 02:09:52.160
Well, it's time for me to tap out.


02:09:52.394 --> 02:09:54.556
Maybe I should
take a page out of Barton's book.


02:09:54.714 --> 02:09:57.638
Build Pepper a farm,
hope nobody blows it up.


02:09:58.434 --> 02:09:59.595
The simple life.


02:09:59.874 --> 02:10:02.161
- You'll get there one day.
- I don't know.


02:10:02.394 --> 02:10:04.795
Family, stability...


02:10:05.954 --> 02:10:09.083
The guy who wanted all that
went in the ice 75 years ago.


02:10:10.594 --> 02:10:12.437
I think someone else came out.


02:10:16.394 --> 02:10:17.475
You all right?


02:10:20.154 --> 02:10:21.599
I'm home.


02:10:29.514 --> 02:10:32.279
You wanna keep staring at the wall,
or do you wanna go to work?


02:10:32.434 --> 02:10:33.765
I mean, it's a pretty interesting wall.


02:10:33.954 --> 02:10:36.958
I thought you and Tony
were still gazing into each other's eyes.


02:10:37.034 --> 02:10:38.081
How do we look?


02:10:38.314 --> 02:10:40.601
Well, we're not the '27 Yankees.


02:10:40.754 --> 02:10:42.438
We got some hitters.


02:10:42.594 --> 02:10:44.995
They're good. They're not a team.


02:10:45.154 --> 02:10:46.804
Let's beat them into shape.


02:11:05.274 --> 02:11:06.799
Avengers...


02:13:25.634 --> 02:13:27.079
Fine.


02:13:28.514 --> 02:13:30.357
I'll do it myself.

